  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="3D Model">
      <data key="d0">3D Model</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The 3D Model refers to a digital representation in three dimensions used in various design and visualization contexts.&lt;SEP&gt;A 3D model represents objects in a three-dimensional space, utilized in Allplan for design and visualization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1679d6e889e44fa43cd8d2680563a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3bf8515f342502ea30e1d362975d491</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896815</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Project Light">
      <data key="d0">Project Light</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Project Light is a method for setting artificial light sources within the 3D model, applicable both inside and outside.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1679d6e889e44fa43cd8d2680563a7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888386</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Camera Path">
      <data key="d0">Camera Path</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Camera Path defines the positions of the camera to create a storyboard for a movie, allowing playback and recording of the movie.&lt;SEP&gt;Camera path refers to options for positioning and navigating the camera view within the design software, enhancing user control over viewport visualization.&lt;SEP&gt;Camera path is another specific functionality in 3D modeling that relates to how users may interact with the Allplan software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1679d6e889e44fa43cd8d2680563a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0b79892ea245e6fed9c92748dc8298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bc5ccd35718eaf0c8bcbb5b6b0ba661</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896705</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Render">
      <data key="d0">Render</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Render calculates photo-realistic bitmaps from the 3D model's current view based on lighting and surface properties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1679d6e889e44fa43cd8d2680563a7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888386</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Record Movie">
      <data key="d0">Record Movie</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Record Movie provides functionality to sequences of animated or rendered bitmaps from the 3D model and save it as an AVI movie.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1679d6e889e44fa43cd8d2680563a7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888386</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Shortcut Menu">
      <data key="d0">Shortcut Menu</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Shortcut Menu is a pivotal component of various design software applications that offers quick access to a variety of tools and functionalities tailored to user interactions. It serves as a context-sensitive menu, adapting its options based on the actions taken by the user and the specific mode of the program being utilized. Within the Objects Palette and Wizards Palette, the Shortcut Menu provides quick access to commonly used commands and functions, enhancing workflow efficiency.

In Allplan, the Shortcut Menu functions as an integral feature, presenting a selection of editing and modification tools. It enables users to enter points, manage geometrical data, and access common editing operations such as 'Undo', 'Cut', 'Copy', 'Paste', 'Delete', and 'Select All'. Additionally, this menu includes functionality for options related to drawing settings, further facilitating user interactions within the design environment.

As a user interface element, the Shortcut Menu not only streamlines access to frequently used tools but also serves as an indicator of potential commands that can be executed based on user gestures, such as right-clicking. Despite its importance, some descriptions highlight that the Shortcut Menu may occasionally lack detailed elaboration, leaving users with a superficial understanding of its full capabilities. Overall, the Shortcut Menu is a crucial feature across design tools, aiming to enhance user experience through efficient navigation and tool accessibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1679d6e889e44fa43cd8d2680563a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f40ac34bd849a8de0bd19474994c664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63113ce4c55fd340029d2a7657821c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef853aad5cd628db1d2c34ebbb5835e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b91a6868a9646c017d41c0d935b68c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfac8b75410f9e9fa0a25fdb3d365c19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0b79892ea245e6fed9c92748dc8298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3e6f28287259d0bcd1778bef739c9fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b6cbdb85b0a4f42ca78c9fb64912931&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1378ad6e2f07b8979f67c396d166ca62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb82ae161313b95f5bb1550ec3b7e9db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e948e86d415daafb0e4b98f95df29b0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21ab5512fed113f2cd711420e2bf6251&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96f432670260a4683e8787869f7b743b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05cb4111eae86b7e402aebcdf6d4efb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3fc8186e7830b562ba8feb86e842109&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9659c8572c987964d5a439769784421b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8f18975f423b4d0916b90c97cb2236c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6da77a5ab4d6187c4da3cb3eaf6de8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-819060699721c575f05e0263ec1086e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dff3ffeae8a699e76e65ae626562059e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f8b5df1347cfcef0c4dd2547d03124&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26eea2337a9b0e6bfc83be0bfb32ac61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22392697d88135ab4dafb424a0ecc181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7b3646c698bb267fd480306b6058059&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df083852a7758df2130fa05bff76c088&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76c676aa485a95ecc906f902ee98664a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9e143bbb0781977a04fcd604ac05e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc08ccbc8c48d9ae4ed2a37be8948adc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b714bcb576d1d7af19a195bad055535&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-498a02f33624e89881923310f78aca92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ad5519a4810cd38a12ea2858647651a</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896713</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Point Snap Options">
      <data key="d0">Point Snap Options</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Point Snap Options enables users to define various types of points for the program to scan in the workspace and set general snap settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Point Snap Options refer to the various settings available in Allplan to configure snapping behaviors and snap radius for drawing.&lt;SEP&gt;Point Snap Options are functionalities in Allplan that help users select specific points for accuracy in design.&lt;SEP&gt;Point Snap Options are functionalities within the design software that can be manipulated, enhancing user interaction.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1679d6e889e44fa43cd8d2680563a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38d959099d4c65fdc7bb2119334ec31e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-867c488f07877357a11b851e2cdc9b03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0fdcae1fb9712e5a27ca1634779dc11</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896722</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Track Tracing Options">
      <data key="d0">Track Tracing Options</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Track Tracing Options allows users to turn track tracing on and off and customize display settings related to track tracing.&lt;SEP&gt;Track Tracing Options allow users to customize the functionality and responsiveness of Track Tracing within the design software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1a1679d6e889e44fa43cd8d2680563a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888386</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Print Preview Palette">
      <data key="d0">Print Preview Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Print Preview Palette is a tool used to configure print settings, including margins, headers, and footers for printouts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Print Preview Palette is a tool in Allplan that allows users to prepare and adjust print settings prior to printing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Print Preview Palette contains settings and options for print customization, including margin definitions and header and footer specifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28f5266d1ec6c127667f218d268add52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc46884d52efdbab23cf1adaae32a9ee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896691</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Printer">
      <data key="d0">Printer</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">A Printer is the output device used for producing hard copies from a computer system.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888387</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Settings">
      <data key="d0">Settings</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Settings refers to the configuration options for the Bimplus project linked with the current Allplan project.&lt;SEP&gt;Settings refer to the configurations available in the Print Preview Palette for adjusting print options.&lt;SEP&gt;Settings refer to the configurations that discuss tasks management and how palettes are integrated into the user experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Settings encompass default values and behaviors that affect element display and ordering.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec22abab62a86e389dc5d86bb0bf9c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a04fbcd66bb19de4cf624f9c31dc42bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14d5b510ef746647b67a2f4d68903a14</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896823</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Margins">
      <data key="d0">Margins</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Margins are configurable spaces around the content in printouts, which can be adjusted using the Print Preview Palette.&lt;SEP&gt;Margins define the printable area of the layout and are crucial for setting up the layout correctly.&lt;SEP&gt;Margins are the blank spaces around the content of a printed document, which can be adjusted to enhance the visual presentation and layout.&lt;SEP&gt;Margins are essential aspects of printing that affect layout and overall output quality in printed documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4206f1947d4ad3d5363e704d586b34d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa75c080b391647ebd8ea4ffd9a169c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0df013c9a633cefb28665d1da2e7dac2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896691</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Header">
      <data key="d0">Header</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Header refers to the area at the top of printed pages where specific content can be displayed or defined.&lt;SEP&gt;Header is a brief title or label intended to introduce a section of content, in this case, the section on layout design and printing processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acac71e2cecd52467bce8878a0b269f0</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896816</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Footer">
      <data key="d0">Footer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Footer refers to the area at the bottom of printed pages where specific content can be displayed or defined.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888387</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layout Editor">
      <data key="d0">Layout Editor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Layout Editor is a tool utilized within Allplan, dedicated to the organization and preparation of design elements intended for presentation or printing. This functionality encompasses a range of tasks including editing layouts, managing layout-specific data, and creating layouts from various documents and filesets before they are sent to print. As part of its features, the Layout Editor allows users to set up page formats, arrange visual elements, and manage printer settings, all of which are essential processes for effective document assembly and customization.

In addition to its use in Allplan, there is also a reference to a Layout Editor component within AutoCAD, which serves a similar purpose of organizing and manipulating layouts for printing or exporting. This indicates that the term "Layout Editor" encompasses multiple applications across different software, though its core functionality remains focused on layout management and preparation.

The Layout Editor functions as a categorized section within the design tools, providing a dedicated space where users can access tools to arrange their layouts efficiently. This tool significantly aids users engaged in layout creation by facilitating the configuration of layout settings and enabling customized document management capabilities. In summary, the Layout Editor is essential for users in design and document preparation workflows, streamlining processes crucial for effective and professional outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4206f1947d4ad3d5363e704d586b34d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a9230f90f86536e2d89709e70964c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-461b65dc8290feb9444a308b8425f47c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfac8b75410f9e9fa0a25fdb3d365c19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1710ee37e8dbe9125820f0b81b80de4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0386115ae26e321feecb48cffce34026&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bb7196cb6473314cea476d85b5ba306&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aefd739a94ccf393ca651e35514b5911&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c50516d099bdc960c3aa6f272e41e8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f0a24dd49d580042467a75770362473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21f7007492689da90de9479ef1f09d6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1116a2756d10f2941c172b307843e3c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0dbb6e05a698136a165e1c1e8e4e2a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f1c1dffb20e9037822fb3685bc70cf</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896652</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Printout">
      <data key="d0">Printout</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A Printout is the final physical copy produced from print settings defined in the Print Preview Palette.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888387</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Printable Area">
      <data key="d0">Printable Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The printable area refers to the maximum area on the page where printing can occur, defined by the margins of the output device.&lt;SEP&gt;The Printable Area refers to the space on a page where content can be printed, determined by the margins and headers/footers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e8ba20e98ba4b0cefedfc63b31256459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4206f1947d4ad3d5363e704d586b34d</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888387</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dialog Line">
      <data key="d0">Dialog Line</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Dialog Line is an essential component of design software, particularly within Computer-Aided Design (CAD) applications. It serves multiple functions, including prompting users to enter values and commands necessary for various operations, which enhances user interaction during the design process. The Dialog Line is particularly notable for its role in facilitating the input of parameters and calculations, making it a fundamental element for designers seeking to set specific measurements or conduct precise adjustments.

As an interface feature, the Dialog Line allows users to specify commands and input length values, effectively acting as a dialog box that supports various interactions within the software. It is characterized by data fields that help in entering measurements, which are crucial for functioning in drafting and design environments. Furthermore, the Dialog Line also provides real-time status updates and prompts, indicating its importance in guiding users throughout their design tasks.

Specifically, the Dialog Line functions as a point entry system labeled 'Δx' in some instances, which underscores its utility in linking user actions to existing points in the design space. It can also be associated with commands that pertain to drawing or measuring lines, reinforcing its integral role in the design workflow.

In summary, the Dialog Line is a versatile and vital interface element in CAD and design software, playing a crucial role in user interaction, parameter input, and measurement functionalities. It enhances the overall efficiency and effectiveness of design processes by providing users with a structured means to communicate their commands and parameters within the software environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f40ac34bd849a8de0bd19474994c664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63113ce4c55fd340029d2a7657821c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56e0d709a61c2954fff181af06317028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81d0a33e22c729229d6fbe523832a15&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8f18975f423b4d0916b90c97cb2236c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6ce70dad379ae311b37a838efcb486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d348a021fa662b95c5f1d68673e66bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26eea2337a9b0e6bfc83be0bfb32ac61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d974a3bc11385c7f6ae0b56664a2ef1</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896723</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Point Assistant">
      <data key="d0">Point Assistant</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Point Assistant is a feature that provides tools and options for entering points and creating elements in the program.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f40ac34bd849a8de0bd19474994c664</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888387</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Carbon-Fiber Spikes">
      <data key="d0">Carbon-Fiber Spikes</data>
      <data key="d1">equipment</data>
      <data key="d2">Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced footwear used to enhance performance in sprinting, showcased in the library's elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced tools used in the application context to enhance performance when creating elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes represent advanced tools enhancing performance in sprinting or athletic applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced sprinting shoes that provide enhanced speed and traction.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced sprinting shoes that enhance speed and traction for athletes.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-Fiber Spikes are advanced components used in athletic footwear to enhance sprinter performance through improved speed and traction.&lt;SEP&gt;Carbon-fiber spikes are advanced sprinting shoes that provide enhanced speed and traction for athletes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f40ac34bd849a8de0bd19474994c664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12df672618de36e5be89afed9ceb5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf93c97b7398da09d1cabc644a3e194&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2705dc98383cde48e236bb2ab1b3a5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dee441f8d4c227560fc9d1685d03ae8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f1c1dffb20e9037822fb3685bc70cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61d38d09f559075f8197b0be943702bc</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896670</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Workspace">
      <data key="d0">Workspace</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Workspace is a central area within the Allplan software environment, serving as the primary interface where users visually manipulate and modify elements based on their input. This designated area allows users to draw and place design elements, including smart symbols and SmartParts, effectively facilitating the design process.

In the Workspace, users can also interact with the Actionbar and other design elements, which provides access to various tools and functions essential for design operations. The Actionbar interface is docked within this environment, enhancing the user's ability to navigate and employ different features, such as wizards and palettes. 

Overall, the Workspace functions as the environment where users carry out their tasks related to the design process, including copying elements from wizards and managing interactions through mouse operations. It constitutes a pivotal part of user interface operations, integrating multiple functionalities to support efficient design workflows.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f40ac34bd849a8de0bd19474994c664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d305d677976b85ecf574260a9460d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7381ee705a6c05c03181833c355e759f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc4489156f7338736e4a38b8b10cc98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dff3ffeae8a699e76e65ae626562059e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58b8c205c8612c072166b688afee2ede&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a3c6573a5b9569603e459e21f12e7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dfb51c08102b928e5de30c60482227e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d1b4de497a5fe1b10fc18b07af2d409&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df083852a7758df2130fa05bff76c088</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896711</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Input Tools">
      <data key="d0">Input Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Input tools refer to the various mechanisms available to enter values, points, and configurations in the program.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f40ac34bd849a8de0bd19474994c664</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888387</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Grid Dimensions">
      <data key="d0">Grid Dimensions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Grid dimensions are measurements that allow users to place points and elements with precision in architectural elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Grid Dimensions are mentioned as part of the surrounding context that discusses functionalities within the interface, though not detailed.&lt;SEP&gt;Grid Dimensions are measurements that provide a structured layout for drawing, essential for ensuring accuracy in architectural design.&lt;SEP&gt;Grid Dimensions refer to the parameters used for accurately managing space in architectural drafting.&lt;SEP&gt;Grid Dimensions are concepts described in the surrounding content that capitalize on the foundational knowledge introduced in the discarded section.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f40ac34bd849a8de0bd19474994c664&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d441d934a4907cd1da742212fdab339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbc7e19fe5f9d99f4b190011e5d5a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9706d9f8ff5f5b9f5468aaffbe1ce7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12af230f97935fb21664cc17d2d00177</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896802</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Z-Direction">
      <data key="d0">Z-Direction</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Z-Direction refers to the vertical axis in a three-dimensional space, used for placing points and elements where required.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-6f40ac34bd849a8de0bd19474994c664</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888388</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Allplan 2020">
      <data key="d0">Allplan 2020</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Allplan 2020 is a high-performance Computer-Aided Design (CAD) software specifically tailored for architects and civil engineers. This version of Allplan comes equipped with a suite of advanced tools and functionalities designed for the effective design, modification, and management of construction elements. As the latest iteration in the Allplan software lineage, users can expect new features aimed at enhancing architectural and engineering workflows.

The software is characterized by its comprehensive installation requirements, which include guidelines on system specifications to ensure optimal performance. It can be installed either as a viewer or as a fully functional application, depending on the user's need. Detailed user guidance is provided within the software's documentation, offering instructions on installation procedures, user interface elements, and operational commands relevant to both standalone and network setups.

Allplan 2020 is also significant in discussions surrounding data exchange and layout management, making it a pivotal tool in architectural modeling and documentation processes. Moreover, it is designed to facilitate user navigation through a structured interface that highlights essential tools for construction layout and planning tasks.

The documentation accompanying Allplan 2020 emphasizes installation processes, user guidance, and functionalities related to printing and layout management. However, several mentions of "discarded content" indicate there are sections lacking substantial context or detailed information about specific features or updates, which might limit users' understanding of the software's complete capabilities. The software version has been referenced in discussions surrounding viewport controls, project management tools, and compatibility with Building Information Modeling (BIM) systems.

Allplan 2020 also relates to architectural design tools concerning layout design and printing functionalities. It aims to guide users through the various data representation techniques while offering configurations for print layouts. Despite some gaps in detailed exposition found in the documentation, Allplan 2020 remains a crucial resource in the CAD landscape, addressing the needs of professionals involved in architectural design and construction planning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b9dc41165ce839cf3f850050abd7081e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aef18e4906ae04faffda048cb70ce961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8deeda22c4730643daae705342beefc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daf5eae8ae425042459bcc9090c9b4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e268c5fca383ae514500af3364494c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81cf5c85be9f4469f5b46f9f3d23dc66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05e5481e89f4d2db7d1cdb8be7ef7ee0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ec753005c525b36946a5dabcfec6f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-696b895267139307fa5be3f42205931a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5524a804838c54b1bc6356af1c661a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd9aa94aab594fbf7969b531d375552&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc13dda0d7c0c2c54fe77ac05d35e6f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d91ff5bf9a308f02afa133830a8149bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575527346b06bf6c21d3b7006a63ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6afa5f759d7f8c642dec36a4e71def5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c83c1aef60ad63396f927675cd8127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b145be60bd5b4836d449304a39810d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba383c530828b33ba426182587f02182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db6f7c98c11e54d08745377d700d7095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f02f6b3b8e4f1161b81a66ae45197197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44248d42ce4be34f917e4803c9fa3d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74a2eaeea310538229b74b8eed7752ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9c590d5431137797758c5eabaea4c91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a8a82f299e74e7da1ede2ee18ded75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81ac7e813a6b1a76ec1f33fc619ade62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a9714aa009a544e12d91b6e75a4d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edbad0848ac1658c95cc5a602785920d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7bdb96e13975902eb2689a443344067&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0d0286b52a38d14145fcd7a7ed59cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55fc07062252f4c1c4c435c8b418f9dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f8bf95246eac0b69dee2f7567075fc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2f4b50f91a440267fc0fa54988276d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e0542c18310ce20a17cad3616ccfa80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a145ff34e1fe0d010deba2fca752fde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4adef92f9cbb80ea2c93efad2f10f24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0b79892ea245e6fed9c92748dc8298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-841ddeeb367db179e52e136890e7970a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1798a5b98f689569497cc66fb113a34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3369cc16fc27c6f1fecd6f710043f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a8f0f6485303