      <data key="d5">1763888388</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="NPL Files">
      <data key="d0">NPL Files</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">NPL files are referenced in Allplan as a type of file used alongside NDW files for document management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a16b1e5756a6e58b24d2d8ec53fdb945</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888388</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Filesets">
      <data key="d0">Filesets</data>
      <data key="d1">component</data>
      <data key="d2">Filesets are collections of drawing files organized within a project in Allplan, allowing for structured design management.&lt;SEP&gt;Filesets are categorized within the selected folder in the ProjectPilot tool, aiding in the organization of project data.&lt;SEP&gt;Filesets refers to a node in the file tree, highlighting a collection of grouped files or folders within the software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a16b1e5756a6e58b24d2d8ec53fdb945&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b12ac308c348c167a0c3b407e59a72a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4633e4c71d2db6ddf873662d52285a65</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layouts">
      <data key="d0">Layouts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Layouts are the units in Allplan that organize and prepare drawing files for printing and presentation purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Layouts refer to the arrangement of documents within the software that can be exported in various formats like DXF, DWG, or DGN.&lt;SEP&gt;Layouts are arrangements or designs concerning the organization of elements within a project, relevant to managing visual designs and files.&lt;SEP&gt;Layouts are part of the contents displayed in the Architecture Tutorial (with Model) folder in the ProjectPilot tool.&lt;SEP&gt;Layouts pertain to the arrangements and designs that can be created within Allplan 2020 for printing purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Layouts are arrangements of printing settings and functionalities within Allplan 2020, affecting how designs are outputted.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a16b1e5756a6e58b24d2d8ec53fdb945&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ca43a5078c0cb201783352641cc976&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b145be60bd5b4836d449304a39810d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db6f7c98c11e54d08745377d700d7095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe9f0600b71ac1fb6333f1bc72307a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b12ac308c348c167a0c3b407e59a72a8</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896681</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Project Templates">
      <data key="d0">Project Templates</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Project templates are predefined projects in Allplan that can be used as a basis for creating new projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Project templates are critical aspects discussed in conjunction with file management and are necessary for effective usage in organizing projects and documents.&lt;SEP&gt;Project Templates are structures that guide the organization of project-related information and documentation, relevant to managing drawing files.&lt;SEP&gt;Project Templates are mentioned as part of ongoing processes within project management, likely involving standardized structures for project creation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a16b1e5756a6e58b24d2d8ec53fdb945&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4012b27b6c7c8ef787dad7737712bf80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18edc46e5a18f23cf88cbe8064760df9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-560d69182ab5365b678a148d9b6e2e37</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Building Structure">
      <data key="d0">Building Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Building Structure is a pivotal concept within the Allplan software, designed to enhance the organization and management of architectural projects. It refers to the hierarchical arrangement and organization of elements within a construction project, allowing for a logical framework that supports the design and layout. This structure facilitates various advantages and applications in design by providing a customizable and flexible system for managing drawing files and associated data.

Building Structure encompasses the physical form and components of a building, serving as the foundation for modeling and analysis within Allplan. It is characterized by its comprehensive approach to organizing and managing various building components, encompassing methodologies that emphasize structured levels and the automatic generation of drawing files. The framework aids in efficient architectural documentation and design processes, aligning with regulatory standards necessary for functional construction.

Additionally, the Building Structure discusses the broader architectural discourse surrounding the physical organization and construction methodologies related to erecting buildings. This includes the importance of having a structured organizational framework that encapsulates both physical systems and design elements. The concept extends to the management of administrative documents and tools, ensuring that the building's design can be effectively executed and adhered to during construction.

In summary, the Building Structure represents a fundamental aspect of architectural design, integrating both theoretical and practical components that enhance the overall functionality, design integrity, and regulatory compliance within construction endeavors using Allplan software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a16b1e5756a6e58b24d2d8ec53fdb945&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83ed2f4c4b8b09ff37fd8fcc9a82daa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-722696e14943f4546267ecafc68e9e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0433c102924e3e18af2ecc35cca067d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2531b166525237884bbbf813c7b6ce26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c3001bb4f90b328d07bc0d87be68f96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0da4f54485b9020eccb0b77b54a99b86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67dfee589c53dba42a267369b0e004d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c58dcec495eda4f7d4331fe428057b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d229ff07439ada86c42a9e43bdaccd9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-462a215f688505a6b73993f7d3e01da9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9f6b783df3aaef7ef959310de966c1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce8d79e428abfeb823efb39b4912455d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96f1266002cbc58170c89b43e5a6ce03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9495a874a42e0e74b1c55ba2281e15c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93bf0628b8070762c9ab05449b3598c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c36318c700d8e026eded8b42d35c63ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9add4b1a1710511eb95f28026e2db24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-895e7a5e80f106b50d21886d5083d4c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f6c404c64e4b1ed54d44fbd63a41fb7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896728</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ProjectPilot">
      <data key="d0">ProjectPilot</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">ProjectPilot is a comprehensive data management tool integrated within Allplan 2020, designed to facilitate the effective management of project elements and documentation throughout the design process. It serves various functionalities such as managing project templates, where users can delete or rename templates stored in the office folder, as well as handling project documentation to enhance workflow efficiency.

Key features of ProjectPilot include robust tools for creating, structuring, and organizing project data. This includes capabilities for copying, moving, renaming, and deleting data, which are essential for maintaining accurate and organized project information. The tool also aids in managing properties associated with project elements, making it easier for users to access and manipulate relevant data.

In addition to data management, ProjectPilot offers functionalities related to document editing and management, which encompass a variety of operational tasks such as sorting and searching through documents, as well as navigating project folders. The software also supports layer management and may involve features related to controlling access rights for users, ensuring that data organization adheres to project requirements.

Moreover, ProjectPilot likely includes installation procedures and basic operational guidelines to assist users in fully utilizing its advanced features. Though it is primarily focused on data management, the tool also emphasizes the importance of best practices for efficient usage. As such, it is seen as an essential component for managing architectural project data and structural drawing files, helping users maintain a clear overview of design elements necessary for effective project development. 

Overall, ProjectPilot stands as a versatile software tool that enhances the experience of managing architectural and engineering projects within the Allplan ecosystem, streamlining workflows, and fostering organized data handling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a16b1e5756a6e58b24d2d8ec53fdb945&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef853aad5cd628db1d2c34ebbb5835e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a840120e862e758547b6c08892ccdfa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fa2ac25e8d82137090e36aeea955a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b94a77849dcec033c128c7bbe00e460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b12ac308c348c167a0c3b407e59a72a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56bfdccc38d0d737c25f01ffe802f1b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f78e4728c1e587ce40447f58ca512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b12e158fa506ce1a47cfc505d9f8a87e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09cc853c0929848d59ac804c43580402&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d67011f7a75a85372a25d4ae9f8c2a38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f0bf0e417fea1a9524c7b394e0c83c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c8c77938fe1ab87d321fb80c43e74aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f22c7d4278cd63fdbd7cf9330981f92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2eccf72f009f59271d4816c6146faae2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c9e2758aa6ea4365a71c4ece076640a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0bc7d14abd3d60dc45c8a51bce1f5a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e81eca64c42f550b12f0f82c5610f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65c4da9217dc97505bc84408f2584901&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4901dd049e53e11bac440c0a18ad69bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eacd30458304f4a54f67ca104596362e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c65fc1384050cd18915c35e7f2ebc24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3ecf5c3adbf9325efc01db9c8bd48aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d084f8d91bd7ea701e82581899432ab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6c7b27b30480dab8361768f8b225f5</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896857</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hierarchical Levels">
      <data key="d0">Hierarchical Levels</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hierarchical levels refer to the logical structuring of a building's data in Allplan, essential for forming a Building Information Model (BIM).</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a16b1e5756a6e58b24d2d8ec53fdb945</data>
