    </node>
    <node id="User">
      <data key="d0">User</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The User, as described, represents individuals engaging with the Allplan software for various design and editing tasks. Users interact with features such as viewports, printing options, and the Layout Editor, indicating their need for proficiency with the application to enhance their design workflow.

Users typically engage with Allplan 2020, often utilizing the User Manual to deepen their understanding of the software's functionalities. They require a foundational knowledge of installation processes and the overall capabilities of the software to navigate effectively. In addition, the concept of the User encompasses those who may not be fully aware of certain features, particularly how the absence of certain content can affect navigation and operational efficiency.

Furthermore, the term User is also associated with specific functionalities within the software, such as the Attribute Selection dialog box, which manages user-specific attributes pertinent to building structures. This illustrates the broad applicability of the term, as it encompasses users involved in both basic tasks and those engaging with advanced capabilities. 

Overall, Users of Allplan are individuals who vary in their familiarity with the software, but all share the necessity for guidance in installation and usage to optimize their experience and productivity within the application.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63113ce4c55fd340029d2a7657821c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a9714aa009a544e12d91b6e75a4d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6be10947dcfd65f1fff0182709649f1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0c100b013d9494004b8d5886c9ede3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2938bd952ac9fb2a762941c3969e71e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4980fca212b3553bb986b694641f509&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f14ba11e1f679acb08cf8352f039503f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67c6ea0408b17c90bee1fa53b6dc7503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da5aa20233e436f7eddf22a9ccca947e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e54809382d7a16c184591f1d6ef4fb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff60d8c24018330ad5d1f786c1f8145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f694199f09ad57655300ad9493ce164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-578e3db6d41d42574729c44d3fde6a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fa30709ea511dd65978c34d2c2d2663</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896696</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Editing Tools">
      <data key="d0">Editing Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Editing Tools are tools available in the Shortcut Menu that allow users to modify and manage design elements within Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Editing Tools refer to the various options available in Allplan for modifying and managing design elements within projects.&lt;SEP&gt;The editing tools are features within the menu, including functions such as 'Wall', 'Match', 'Delete', 'Move', 'Rotate', and 'Copy' for basic manipulations.&lt;SEP&gt;Editing Tools encompass software features that are activated through mouse usage, distinguishing them from standard mouse functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Editing tools refer to the instruments and functionalities discussed in the content across Pages 175 and 177 for element manipulation and geometric properties adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-63113ce4c55fd340029d2a7657821c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5284ab6f8d3848eb3123773ca4bfa0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d43cb4b0d1bfb0415f58fff4033f1de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3c2130d3d4faa7b4c250d2efa11d751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71c4b3de3655872a3d291aba676daaee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896699</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Output Device">
      <data key="d0">Output Device</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">An output device refers to the printer or device used to produce a hard copy of the layout.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4206f1947d4ad3d5363e704d586b34d</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888389</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Print Layouts">
      <data key="d0">Print Layouts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Print Layouts is a method used to print the assembled layouts and can specify various settings including the output device.&lt;SEP&gt;Print layouts refer to predefined formats used for printing documents and are managed through a specific editor task in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Print Layouts refer to the arrangement and design of printed materials, which is part of the broader discussion on optimizing print outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Print Layouts is a feature within a printing application that manages various printing configurations and options for users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4206f1947d4ad3d5363e704d586b34d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-451be9692297c28020f54c8273fd6dca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c757f29b0cc6308adb48eda300c33068&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a343a102418944f180cb878a7f0977c1</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896820</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PDF File">
      <data key="d0">PDF File</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A PDF File is a digital document format that can be created from the layouts for distribution or archival purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4206f1947d4ad3d5363e704d586b34d</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888389</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Rasterize Length">
      <data key="d0">Rasterize Length</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Rasterize Length is a setting that activates grid dimensions and influences how lengths are defined within design software.&lt;SEP&gt;Rasterize Length is a function within the software that activates grid dimensions or adjusts granularity for design purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Rasterize Length refers to a feature mentioned in the context of installation basics, highlighting its significance for architectural tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a006a6c963e8781295b7d58c913f54fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbc7e19fe5f9d99f4b190011e5d5a6c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896802</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Track Lines">
      <data key="d0">Track Lines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Track Lines refer to a set of tools available within the Allplan software that facilitate precision drawing and enhance efficiency in architectural design. These functionalities are critical for guiding dimensions in layouts, allowing users to create accurate graphical elements such as walls. Track Lines provide visual guidance, making the drawing process more intuitive and time-efficient by aiding in the alignment of various design components.

Distinct types of Track Lines include extension, orthogonal, polar, and perpendicular lines, each contributing to the design process by offering different forms of guidance. These functional elements assist users in managing and creating graphical paths, thereby improving overall drafting efficiency. When integrated into workflows, Track Lines can enhance the accuracy of designs by clearly specifying lengths and snapping points, ensuring that elements are aligned precisely.

Upon successful installation of the Allplan software, users can leverage these advanced features effectively, as they are designed to be intuitive and user-friendly. Furthermore, Track Lines are discussed in connection with operational tips aimed at optimizing design workflows, illustrating their importance in the drafting phase of projects. Overall, Track Lines are essential elements within design software that significantly contribute to improving the quality and efficiency of architectural outputs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-722696e14943f4546267ecafc68e9e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b5cf406cd697c419102aea78243d839&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b5581edd6a5150ce2ec40420195a45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c32800b93fbfcf403671e77c76a3080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b671bba7089145f32ec4ba1a3653bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2f14b0688cfc85627075749179d292fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-450a009effcf289fffe7290019181323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baebfe93afc0212656ba8acaf7af18ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-798c3d5bcda492510a7e0347ecda7791&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69e09c63a8c64b12f235e7d39ceeb1f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2f543da2f86d69390c850f7f9ff2fbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-486fae4c137be122764c551c6470c78c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ed739e34b8ee76c942aff4971bffbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6610c85a94e09076a70b7846eb987c6</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896811</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Basic Dimensions">
      <data key="d0">Basic Dimensions</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Basic Dimensions refer to a predefined set of measurements that can be used in design applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Basic Dimensions is one of the options available within the Dimension Drop-Down Menu, representing a type of dimension setting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121d2b678516eaba15f9dd3dcee2a570</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896803</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Outside Dimensions">
      <data key="d0">Outside Dimensions</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Outside Dimensions are a specific type of measurement option available in design software for defining the outer limits of an object.&lt;SEP&gt;Outside Dimensions is another option within the Dimension Drop-Down Menu, indicating measurements related to the exterior of a structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121d2b678516eaba15f9dd3dcee2a570</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896803</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Opening Dimensions">
      <data key="d0">Opening Dimensions</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Opening Dimensions are measurements that pertain to the openings within a design, providing necessary specifications in layout design.&lt;SEP&gt;Opening Dimensions is a type of measurement setting available in the Dimension Drop-Down Menu, focusing on dimensions for openings in design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-121d2b678516eaba15f9dd3dcee2a570</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896803</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ToolTip">
      <data key="d0">ToolTip</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A ToolTip is a user interface element that provides additional information regarding a particular functionality within the software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Construction Lines">
      <data key="d0">Construction Lines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Construction Lines are temporary lines used in design to assist in the layout and alignment of elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Construction Lines are traditional design elements that may be eliminated through the use of track lines, thereby improving design efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ff1607eea6829dfcc8901492384569</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896807</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Perpendicular">
      <data key="d0">Perpendicular</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Perpendicular refers to a feature in design software that helps users create angles of 90 degrees relative to existing elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Parallel Line">
      <data key="d0">Parallel Line</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Parallel Line is a tool in design software used to create lines that run alongside and at equal distances from existing elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Track Points">
      <data key="d0">Track Points</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Track Points are specific markers in design software that help with snapping and alignment during element placement.&lt;SEP&gt;Track Points are elements within the design software that can be deleted, as discussed in the document's instructions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0fdcae1fb9712e5a27ca1634779dc11</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896725</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="3D Solids">
      <data key="d0">3D Solids</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">3D Solids are three-dimensional objects in design software that can be manipulated and are integral to creating complex designs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c43949300eb25c19d8895e4becd1bdee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Allplan Exchange">
      <data key="d0">Allplan Exchange</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Allplan Exchange is a tool for distributing electronic documents over the internet.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ALLPLAN GmbH">
      <data key="d0">ALLPLAN GmbH</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">ALLPLAN GmbH is the organization responsible for creating the ALLPLAN software and associated documentation.&lt;SEP&gt;ALLPLAN GmbH is the developer of Bimplus, focusing on building data exchanges in the architecture and engineering sectors.&lt;SEP&gt;ALLPLAN GmbH is a company based in Munich, known for publishing the ALLPLAN 2020 Manual and holding copyright over its content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-622bc0a81d4bbd6eb8e804c4463c94f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4b739d9230f8a76c068c9c1cd2c1f2e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896732</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Welcome Screen">
      <data key="d0">Welcome Screen</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Welcome Screen is a feature in Allplan that displays recent projects and can be turned off if desired.&lt;SEP&gt;The Welcome Screen is a feature of the Allplan user interface that provides users with an introduction to the software's functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Welcome Screen is a header indicating a section about the Welcome Screen feature in Allplan software, providing access to tools for project creation and opening.&lt;SEP&gt;The Welcome Screen is where various features and functionalities can be accessed in the Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;The Welcome Screen is a minimalistic content element that introduces the Allplan software but lacks detailed exposition and relevance.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ffeae8062640bc4344c3b7beb9ec8aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d38d6185475b7afa04ee148f69ebcec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a96e049ecada2a58e9cb999bfcd0afb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ee381f225589a5bc5741093a94e267b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896850</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Default Configurations">
      <data key="d0">Default Configurations</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Default Configurations refer to the pre-set user interface settings available in Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888390</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Working Area">
      <data key="d0">Working Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Working Area is part of the Allplan interface where users can manage controls and view their projects.&lt;SEP&gt;The Working Area is the primary space within the software application where users perform their tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Working Area is a part of the Allplan window that allows users to engage with various project components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5efc6fb4de4f5c15827fe552ce16b42</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896852</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Quick Access Toolbar">
      <data key="d0">Quick Access Toolbar</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Quick Access Toolbar (QAT) is a key feature within Allplan software that enhances user experience by providing immediate and customizable access to frequently used tools and commands. Designed to streamline workflow, the QAT allows users to arrange their essential tools conveniently, ensuring that important functionalities are always within reach while working on design projects.

As a customizable element of Allplan's user interface, the Quick Access Toolbar facilitates personalization, allowing users to tailor the tools displayed based on their specific needs. This customization promotes efficiency in project management and drawing organization, as users can quickly find and utilize tools relevant to their tasks without navigating through multiple menus.

Moreover, the Quick Access Toolbar plays a significant role in user manuals and tutorials, serving as a focal point for educating users on interface personalization and maximizing efficiency. By integrating the QAT into their workflow, users can optimize their use of the Allplan application, ultimately improving their productivity and project outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b532fa4a8ab92ded3fea1d57304eeffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712ac7e367720bf0768cb3b167957363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-415ff18941e50c38a3c2c67a308d09fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-575138ede49e6b4257478409c025e498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a244da62e429c7705c53c4c5a40d7e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd9d2bd312f0f22d9ffc3359290a59fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4faf10764600594e5d98531e142dd907&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d099869dd762f58622ec8ec268721766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4cbb8c7ca0283957c1c36f9d33a212&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cfbdcd286fb30bd430a5f20fdd1dcf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecda41be318a51a07214b73099fcb56a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3c2130d3d4faa7b4c250d2efa11d751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ea3cf9156a4c203bc69b1b2c68207c7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896846</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Edit Tool">
      <data key="d0">Edit Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">component</data>
      <data key="d2">The Edit Tool allows users to access general editing functions familiar from other Windows applications within Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;An edit tool is a function in Allplan that allows users to perform various operations on selected elements, like copying or modifying them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888391</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Print Preview Tool">
      <data key="d0">Print Preview Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Print Preview Tool in Allplan enables users to view how their project will print before finalizing the printout.&lt;SEP&gt;The Print Preview Tool is a feature within Allplan 2020 that allows users to view print settings before actually printing.&lt;SEP&gt;The Print Preview Tool is a feature allowing users to visualize and customize print layouts before actual printing, with various options available for document presentation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Print Preview tool allows users to navigate, adjust settings, and interact with various elements for printout configurations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d44248d42ce4be34f917e4803c9fa3d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc46884d52efdbab23cf1adaae32a9ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c31e31141db6176b58736c753cf2db2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896684</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Undo Tool">
      <data key="d0">Undo Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Undo Tool is used in Allplan to revert one or more actions, except for changes made in dialog boxes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Undo Tool allows users to revert actions in the Allplan software, as detailed on page 32 of the Allplan Manual.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d863cf56d52a0a84c6c2cd45b83f8506</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896857</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Redo Tool">
      <data key="d0">Redo Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">component</data>
      <data key="d2">The Redo Tool allows users to repeat actions that have just been undone in Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888391</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Allplan Shop">
      <data key="d0">Allplan Shop</data>
      <data key="d1">location</data>
      <data key="d2">The Allplan Shop is an online platform where users can access additional resources and tools related to Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Allplan Shop is accessible via the Title Bar, providing additional features or resources for users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-87aecad85380c390cbc2374858405d69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5efc6fb4de4f5c15827fe552ce16b42</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896852</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Fileset Structure">
      <data key="d0">Fileset Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The fileset structure allows for the creation, modification, and management of filesets associated with drawing files in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Fileset structure refers to the organization of drawing files and their relationships to the structural levels of a building.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83ed2f4c4b8b09ff37fd8fcc9a82daa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888391</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Structural Levels">
      <data key="d0">Structural Levels</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Structural Levels are defined as the various layers or tiers used to logically organize a building within architectural design software, specifically within Allplan. These levels facilitate the assignment of drawing files to specific tiers, which is crucial for managing the structural components of a building effectively.

The concept of Structural Levels encompasses predefined or custom layers essential for the organization and management of various aspects of a building’s design and implementation. These layers represent different hierarchies within a building structure that must be accounted for during the construction process. Each level can have associated restrictions and implications, particularly within the framework of Building Information Modeling (BIM) practices, where height adjustments and usability of design files are impacted.

In a practical context, Structural Levels are intertwined with the construction stages represented in architectural models, where specific height values correspond to the displayed layout. They play a vital role in discussions around building design and management processes, influencing technical decisions made during design projects.

Overall, Structural Levels are fundamental for the organized depiction and manipulation of building frameworks in architectural rendering and construction planning, contributing to the comprehensive understanding of building hierarchies, layers, and related functionalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83ed2f4c4b8b09ff37fd8fcc9a82daa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-900dab27472a9806ed3ac086b9249508&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdea26b8c5364ac43c1e1ce6ec4898e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57c9f87c2506a2e37df6faf46470d7d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a391cb4a4c94fa59fc6f439fea9eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2178b2cb7ae5eb73332368dadd64d9a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03bd8810ab0f5a641111f6afa525d25c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3347e46b091e6d44734f25df9aa8eb3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3562d6726fa0bbac3b7eebc748987816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed59463fa8f100574963a839714cf2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933be2e47badf7d524c23679977b9769&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be1782cf19027851f94de5abece6998</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896734</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="IFC">
      <data key="d0">IFC</data>
      <data key="d1">dataformat</data>
      <data key="d2">IFC refers to Industry Foundation Classes, a data model used for facilitating data exchange in building design, which can be incorporated into the structural levels in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC stands for Industry Foundation Classes, defining an object-oriented data model used for data exchange in the building process.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC refers to Industry Foundation Classes, a standard used for data management and interoperability within the architecture, engineering, and construction industries.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC (Industry Foundation Classes) is an open data format used for building and construction data organization and management.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC is a widely used file format for data exchange in architecture, notably for building information modeling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-83ed2f4c4b8b09ff37fd8fcc9a82daa6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ca43a5078c0cb201783352641cc976&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dee441f8d4c227560fc9d1685d03ae8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4762118b47b3857f33c900be29277bd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce8d79e428abfeb823efb39b4912455d</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896669</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
