    <node id="Clipboard">
      <data key="d0">Clipboard</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The clipboard is a feature in Allplan that allows users to copy and insert elements into drawing files or other applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Clipboard is a temporary storage area for data that the user wants to copy from one place to another.&lt;SEP&gt;The Clipboard is a feature that allows users to copy and paste data within the user interface of the software application.&lt;SEP&gt;Clipboard is a functionality in Allplan that allows users to copy and paste elements within the software, with specific restrictions on certain elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Clipboard refers to a temporary storage area used for cut, copy, and paste operations in computing environments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Clipboard is a temporary storage area where data is held during operations such as 'Copy', 'Cut', and 'Paste' within Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03a9230f90f86536e2d89709e70964c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b59ad7c2058f9c98f3cb5ca94ce8561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f26419be6bf0d190e1b94afae37c7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b3cfd01962c5039b7d5a5516f5d8ae0a</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896811</data>
