    <node id="Handles">
      <data key="d0">Handles</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Handles are interactive elements employed in the Allplan software that serve as colored symbols appearing at designated points on selected graphical elements. These features are integral to the user interface design, facilitating geometric modifications and adjustments of the design components in the software environment.

Specifically, handles allow users to directly interact with and manipulate elements, providing visual cues that enhance user engagement. They can change color and behavior based on user interaction, which helps in indicating editable options. Furthermore, handles are adjustable, with their characteristics potentially varying according to installation processes.

Overall, handles are crucial for enabling effective modifications within the design space of Allplan, thereby supporting the user in achieving specific design goals through intuitive adjustments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-82cbcdc0a3c08b89e366f56c7b12be7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a007e42b9b683c4bb5c145f80014d5b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e9d61277a96d80b385e938a7ed48f4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36a48bd4ff2dfa611c2ab3b1feafc1da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e272a0453cd6a3118ca7ab3fcea51f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99a31b03d7ae632f5932ec2916b58d47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4208de824f243ef15b5f0dff38558ef7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80fa3a37f0318fe30f8600bb7535a383</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896895</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Entry Boxes">
      <data key="d0">Entry Boxes</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Entry Boxes in Allplan allow users to input values to define the geometry of selected elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Entry Boxes are components in a user interface that enable user input and interaction with the application.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-82cbcdc0a3c08b89e366f56c7b12be7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80fa3a37f0318fe30f8600bb7535a383</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896895</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Direct Object Modification">
      <data key="d0">Direct Object Modification</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Direct Object Modification is a prominent feature in Allplan software that enables users to alter design elements directly within the workspace. This functionality allows for immediate editing following the selection of design entities, thereby enhancing productivity and streamlining the design process. 

The capabilities of Direct Object Modification include various manipulations such as moving, rotating, mirroring, and copying elements, all designed to facilitate quick adjustments and refinements in design projects. Users can directly interact with objects using multiple selection methods, which contributes to greater efficiency in editing tasks.

Additionally, Direct Object Modification incorporates the use of handles and properties within the software interface, making it easier for users to change or edit design elements seamlessly. This technique is essential for user understanding and effective utilization of Allplan's editing features, as it empowers users to make modifications directly in their design environment. 

Overall, Direct Object Modification plays a crucial role in the operation of Allplan software, highlighting its importance as a topic of discussion regarding the software's capabilities in design alteration.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-82cbcdc0a3c08b89e366f56c7b12be7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03833b31b2891d602b91a99573458723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d22aa3727584f0915cfc570314a93e86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f938b002183643b02e96ec9c3db44d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2c57b3e6ef820340af49795681771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e36969f4f63b7e40cff66adc31e252fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e7aefa49736130484d0aa9eb879db55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c7cee9ed314b60a905e2cb7ec4a1095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8b4b49dc911641e02044d82a2b296fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-985fa1397e7d09f51820584ab96aec42</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896893</data>
      <data key="d6" />
