    <node id="Changing Direction">
      <data key="d0">Changing Direction</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Changing Direction is a feature that allows users to apply changes to linear elements either to the left, right, or both sides.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-82cbcdc0a3c08b89e366f56c7b12be7c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Locking or Unlocking the Angle">
      <data key="d0">Locking or Unlocking the Angle</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Locking or Unlocking the Angle enables users to maintain or change the inclination angle of an element relative to the horizontal.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-82cbcdc0a3c08b89e366f56c7b12be7c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Allplan">
      <data key="d0">Allplan</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Allplan is a comprehensive software solution extensively utilized in architectural design and engineering project management. It serves as a vital tool for professionals in these domains, offering a multitude of functionalities such as computer-aided design (CAD), project management, and building information modeling (BIM). The software equips users with a user-friendly interface and a variety of tools for managing and modifying project layouts, which include options for arranging and editing design elements like symbols and library components. It also features viewport management, allowing precise control over attributes such as pen thickness, colors, line types, and more, thereby ensuring customized design outputs.

Additionally, Allplan supports advanced functionalities for data import and export in multiple formats, including the Industry Foundation Classes (IFC) interface, facilitating efficient data transfer in architectural contexts. Its capabilities extend to automating workflows and creating parametric shapes through visual scripting, enhancing productivity. Allplan’s integration with collaborative systems such as Bimplus aids in project tracking and teamwork efficiency, allowing users to manipulate design entities directly while managing drawing files effectively.

Installation and foundational operations of Allplan are crucial, with structured documentation available to assist users in understanding the basics of installation and software functionality. Allplan emphasizes the importance of managing project structures, including OLE objects and XRefs, which bolster its functionalities for architectural and engineering designs. The software includes tutorials and guides that navigate through its features, making it accessible even for novice users.

In parallel, Allplan is recognized for its focus on efficient file management and interoperability with external software, leveraging various data exchange formats including DWG, DXF, and DGN. This integration underscores its capacity for document management and data import/export tasks, aimed at enhancing user engagement in architectural processes. Furthermore, it supports the use of smart symbols and parametric modeling tools, enabling architects and engineers to define dynamic areas and optimize workflows using libraries and preset defaults. 

Notably, the version of Allplan discussed—Allplan 2020—highlights a reiteration of enhanced structuring for architectural design frameworks, making the software indispensable for managing drawing files within project-specific environments. Overall, Allplan stands out as a sophisticated platform that intricately blends design, data management, and project structuring tools to improve efficiency in architectural practices.</data>
