    </node>
    <node id="Height Settings">
      <data key="d0">Height Settings</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Height settings are parameters that define the vertical dimensions of default planes within a building structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Height settings are specific measurements or configurations related to the design of building structures mentioned in the document.&lt;SEP&gt;Height Settings relates to the attributes adjusted for default planes in a program for building structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ed59463fa8f100574963a839714cf2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933be2e47badf7d524c23679977b9769</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896740</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Default Planes">
      <data key="d0">Default Planes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Default planes are preset reference planes used to establish heights in a building model that can be managed and modified.&lt;SEP&gt;Default Planes are settings within a structure that may influence height and attributes of building designs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-254597cf367b8fd01cc4938f0086ac9a</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896743</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Plane Model">
      <data key="d0">Plane Model</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Plane Model represents a spatial model where reference surfaces can be inserted or modified.&lt;SEP&gt;Plane model is a configuration containing pairs of default planes that define various levels in a building structure.&lt;SEP&gt;A Plane Model is a representation used within design software that can be modified with architectural tools as described in the surrounding content.&lt;SEP&gt;Plane Model refers to a subject within the software environment that is being edited regarding its height settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b91a6868a9646c017d41c0d935b68c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbe3718260bfb37d0523abccfd243ded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-022450438e07746baf3ec21aac40c5b8</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896782</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Project Folder">
      <data key="d0">Project Folder</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Project folder is a designated directory where files associated with a specific project are stored, including building structures and plane models.&lt;SEP&gt;The Project Folder contains project-specific resources in Allplan 2020, indicated by an architectural drawing icon.&lt;SEP&gt;The Project Folder is a directory structure organized for a building project, containing various files and folders for documentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa5fa1a5b5bfcb9299bccb2987fe249f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026f24b87030d011599249910d81669f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896746</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topology Structure">
      <data key="d0">Topology Structure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Topology structure refers to the arrangement of various elements in the building structure that defines connections and relationships among them.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topology Any Structural Level">
      <data key="d0">Topology Any Structural Level</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Topology any structural level signifies any of the possible levels within a building structure that can be defined or assigned various attributes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topology Building">
      <data key="d0">Topology Building</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Topology building relates to the overall structural layout and composition of the entire building in the context of its design and architecture.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topology Story">
      <data key="d0">Topology Story</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Topology story denotes a distinct level or floor within a building structure that can be represented in the overall topology.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topology Substory">
      <data key="d0">Topology Substory</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Topology substory refers to a subordinate level or part of a story within the building structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topology Entire Hierarchy">
      <data key="d0">Topology Entire Hierarchy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Topology entire hierarchy represents the complete organizational structure of the building, encompassing all stories, substories, and levels.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Topology Site">
      <data key="d0">Topology Site</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Topology site pertains to the specific geographical and spatial arrangement where the building structure is located.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-338775c6247efd1422755d0684c5914e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Microsoft Word">
      <data key="d0">Microsoft Word</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Microsoft Word is an OLE server application from which text can be copied to the clipboard.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Microsoft Excel">
      <data key="d0">Microsoft Excel</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Microsoft Excel is another OLE server application that allows users to copy text to the clipboard for pasting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888393</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Elements">
      <data key="d0">Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Elements refer to the design components utilized within the Allplan software, which can be copied, pasted, and manipulated to suit user preferences. These components can vary in type and are governed by specific display sequence rules. Users have the ability to format and modify these individual design elements according to their project requirements.

Within the Allplan interface, Elements constitute a section in the Actionbar, which is a central feature of the software. This section includes various tools related to specific tasks, providing users with access to a collection of tool groups designed for diverse design and modeling processes. The Elements tab is integral to the Actionbar layout, showcasing these tools that facilitate the rendering and management of components based on designated properties.

Overall, Elements serve as the foundational building blocks within Allplan, enabling users to construct and customize designs effectively through their manipulation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6145ea75d080e54922523c67fac964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a1456c27e7c81b4c91906bcd9684b69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2f1c1dffb20e9037822fb3685bc70cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a775f844381c729155776df5489dbcd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14ec08840c3fa4e52e44aa4c6e2af111&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a1878040a560dfbd967a592f92ab0c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-199627324ec70005570ae0ac3cd720b0</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896825</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Design Mode">
      <data key="d0">Design Mode</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Design Mode is a specific operational mode within Allplan software that enables users to access various tools and functionalities essential for designing and editing design entities. This mode is crucial for tasks related to drafting and design, allowing direct interaction with multiple elements such as walls and 3D objects.

In Design Mode, users can create, modify, and manipulate design elements in detail, enhancing their workflow through specialized shortcuts and tools tailored to improve interaction within the software. This operational state also facilitates the configuration and customization of design entities, reinforcing user control over visual representations in their projects.

Design Mode serves as an option for opening and editing projects within the Allplan application, ensuring that users can effectively manage design-related tasks. It emphasizes a focused environment where design functionalities are prioritized, providing a comprehensive interface for drafting elements in a model. Additionally, Design Mode plays a role in controlling display settings during the design process, further integrating various aspects of design management.

Overall, Design Mode is integral to the Allplan design experience, guiding users through design-related instructions while enabling them to engage fully with the available tools and functionalities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2e09e8bba60f1d58ef71be4e357ed2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfac8b75410f9e9fa0a25fdb3d365c19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51a55c1df38fc629e6320598601c7b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a65bf4a9b515ba84da6ad9c94f647d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc4489156f7338736e4a38b8b10cc98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3e6f28287259d0bcd1778bef739c9fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6da77a5ab4d6187c4da3cb3eaf6de8bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f556f8e100c6e0be99790528f7e4185d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da6ca22268421f18038b85c19057c5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96b26f05139721ab6fdfc590ff9aa021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e736c178a87d0b2ebc7335d9f75f28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21db218c2681f002d58d92e06ee2c364&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecec34f9885e0587aea2898f16bd7749&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a98a0ae9b9a97657e6eae4d7f5089ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b714bcb576d1d7af19a195bad055535&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c976e7580ecc2c25da3c8b21bc833be8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93a6b6a1910ba10faa14c33bb8a835c4</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896705</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Navigation Mode">
      <data key="d0">Navigation Mode</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Navigation Mode is a specific functionality within Allplan software that allows users to interactively explore and visualize 3D models without the need to select individual design entities. It emphasizes user movement around the 3D model, facilitating navigation through different sections and functionalities of the application. The primary objective of Navigation Mode is to provide an intuitive environment where users can manipulate the view of the model effectively, concentrating on visualization rather than editing design elements.

In this mode, users employ various navigation tools to navigate through design elements and components, enhancing their understanding of the model’s spatial relationships. The input and interactions are primarily geared toward maneuvering within the 3D space, allowing users to better comprehend the design's overall layout and structure. By categorizing Navigation Mode as a distinct operational facet, Allplan highlights the importance of user interface controls in managing how users engage with the model.

Overall, Navigation Mode serves as a crucial framework that supports users in visualizing and navigating 3D environments, providing an essential tool for effective interaction in design applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2e09e8bba60f1d58ef71be4e357ed2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfac8b75410f9e9fa0a25fdb3d365c19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71a65bf4a9b515ba84da6ad9c94f647d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3e6f28287259d0bcd1778bef739c9fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d7adf0f26ef1d1fb72de6d793184a6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8ad1484fb3bfe252f9c4e5a07b53204&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebf14603361df3e4efb47aa37cf81d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f556f8e100c6e0be99790528f7e4185d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1da6ca22268421f18038b85c19057c5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96b26f05139721ab6fdfc590ff9aa021&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e736c178a87d0b2ebc7335d9f75f28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd2df79f340f25bb5efd673bafb206e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21db218c2681f002d58d92e06ee2c364&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a98a0ae9b9a97657e6eae4d7f5089ed</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="FEA Elements">
      <data key="d0">FEA Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">FEA Elements are design elements in Allplan that cannot be copied to the clipboard.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
