    </node>
    <node id="Allfa Elements">
      <data key="d0">Allfa Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Allfa Elements are another category of design elements in Allplan that cannot be copied to the clipboard.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Bitmap Formats">
      <data key="d0">Bitmap Formats</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Bitmap Formats refer to formats supported for pasting into Allplan from the clipboard, including DIB and WMF.&lt;SEP&gt;Bitmap formats are a type of image format pertinent to the clipboard functionalities in Allplan, highlighting aspects of data handling.&lt;SEP&gt;Bitmap formats relate to the types of graphical representations that can be utilized in clipboard operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11b326d3a55107d559c57ad85195adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4336a77b2c0f73d1d9eceebad911202</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896812</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Color Depth">
      <data key="d0">Color Depth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Color Depth refers to the number of colors displayed in images pasted into Allplan, set to several colors in the context provided.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-62a264c8aef6ec479778e3ef09555fea</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layout Window Tool">
      <data key="d0">Layout Window Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">The Layout Window tool is an easy approach for placing sections of documents within a layout without creating an original layout.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Detailing Windows">
      <data key="d0">Detailing Windows</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">Detailing Windows allow users to display selected elements of a document, working in document mode, or hiding parts of the original.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Crop Layout Task Area">
      <data key="d0">Crop Layout Task Area</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">The Crop Layout task area provides tools to cut an oversized layout into smaller sections for better organization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Document Mode">
      <data key="d0">Document Mode</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Document mode is a working state in which users can interact with sections of documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sequence Defaults Button">
      <data key="d0">Sequence Defaults Button</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">The Sequence Defaults Button is used to modify fixed default values for the sequence in which elements are created or modified.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Surface Elements">
      <data key="d0">Surface Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Surface Elements refer to design aspects that represent the outer area of architectural components, particularly within the Allplan software. These elements encompass various components such as hatching, patterns, fills, and bitmap areas, which are essential for enhancing visual representation in architectural drawings and designs.

In the context of architectural design, Surface Elements are relevant for area measurements and polygonization processes, emphasizing their importance in accurately modeling curved surfaces and other design complexities. They serve as a crucial aspect of the layer management system in Allplan, enabling users to control their visibility and thereby improve the organization of project layouts.

The technical specifications provided by Allplan guide the usage of these Surface Elements, detailing their functionalities and applications. Furthermore, these components can be modified or applied through specific tools, thereby impacting visual representations and facilitating the interaction with various patterns across different design scales.

Overall, Surface Elements play a vital role in architectural design by enhancing the representation of materials and improving the overall aesthetic and functional qualities of architectural projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6145ea75d080e54922523c67fac964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3631f3edd0aa1ec3e63179eafbff6976&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca66e6554489f6f847a5278aa05254a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7460ea58ee99d764421fc3d9f144da87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f19fc9049a6665b44293bf478d8b865&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1979ba0f8d29d8d9c47edf9e866d128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef654b1e3ef63a37895f103aab89d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43da9c48f26a42e9668f66534481e33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-061fb125d2fb8a19e5a7710ea6cde4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-447e96feaa6ad1059f430f86df36d17f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5293b36310b4316d4bc2be440b359ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ad8f9853fc194bce492007ac87533dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17c478a3a7a4228b68608609441cc6e2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896771</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Printer Settings">
      <data key="d0">Printer Settings</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Printer settings vary based on the specific printer model used and must be optimized for best results during printing.&lt;SEP&gt;Printer Settings are options within Allplan 2020 that allow users to configure the printing process according to their preferences.&lt;SEP&gt;Printer Settings refer to the configurable options available for printers that affect printing quality, paper size, and other parameters.&lt;SEP&gt;Printer Settings refer to the configurations that affect the output quality and characteristics of printed materials.&lt;SEP&gt;Printer Settings involve configurations related to how printing processes are managed, including options for layout and color management.&lt;SEP&gt;Printer settings refer to the configurations that need to be adjusted for optimal printing performance.&lt;SEP&gt;Printer Settings refer to the specific adjustments and configurations required for efficient printing operations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a8a82f299e74e7da1ede2ee18ded75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa75c080b391647ebd8ea4ffd9a169c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-097cd422f0a5a69c7792cfb6593af24b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4c802a5c0a2c09d4c065c7399bf6c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37532705642b58daf3a41d1ea239fb42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc05041f2c636650929ac20595ec208b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896686</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Display Sequence">
      <data key="d0">Display Sequence</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Display Sequence determines the order in which elements are shown on the screen based on their properties and creation order.&lt;SEP&gt;Display sequence refers to the order in which elements are arranged visually on the screen based on their defined values.&lt;SEP&gt;Display sequence determines the order in which elements appear on screen, affecting their visibility in the layout.&lt;SEP&gt;Display Sequence is the arrangement of graphical elements that determines how they are rendered on the screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Display Sequence relates to how elements are visually ordered during printing, governed by their creation order and adjustable values.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6145ea75d080e54922523c67fac964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52ac0a5c028fdf26ab60c75009a56a89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e675b87c12904efc6da74808a3b1481</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896816</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Print Layouts Tool">
      <data key="d0">Print Layouts Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Print Layouts Tool in Allplan allows users to manage settings for printing, including pen and color assignments.&lt;SEP&gt;The Print Layouts Tool is a feature in design software that assists users in preparing and managing print layouts for documents.&lt;SEP&gt;The Print Layouts Tool is used to initiate printing directly from the layout editor and allows users to select printing options for elements in the layout.&lt;SEP&gt;The Print Layouts Tool is a software utility used to manage and configure printer output settings in layout designs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1b20c02cb1df7f4a3acfb70d457cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f103e26a10fcd8eb7a7395e3148f3027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c5287c4c8d2cc121dff7af4c8f5b95c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Windows Driver">
      <data key="d0">Windows Driver</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Windows driver is a software component used to control printer settings and manage print jobs for printers like the HP DesignJet 650C.&lt;SEP&gt;The Windows Driver settings affect the printing sequence and can influence how documents and elements are printed from the layout editor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9d383dd8c90a0351bca4303139a1f77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1b20c02cb1df7f4a3acfb70d457cbf</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Coordinate Dialog Box">
      <data key="d0">Coordinate Dialog Box</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Coordinate Dialog Box is a tool used for entering delta values when moving or copying elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The Coordinate Dialog Box is a small interface typically used in CAD or design software for modifying element positions, containing fields for delta values.&lt;SEP&gt;The Coordinate Dialog Box is mentioned as a tool used for modifications in the editing process of elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03833b31b2891d602b91a99573458723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bbc08c2a5e06f66f57db63ec4c7c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54fc5161861531710c469a7ee8a1f087</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896899</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Central Move Handle">
      <data key="d0">Central Move Handle</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Central Move Handle is a feature used for editing and copying elements or groups of elements comprehensively.&lt;SEP&gt;Central Move Handle is a specific handle that facilitates the movement of selected elements within the workspace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03833b31b2891d602b91a99573458723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5f603a18868c143aed40d5faf10d64</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896891</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wizards Palette">
      <data key="d0">Wizards Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Wizards Palette is a distinctive feature within Allplan software, designed to enhance user experience in managing various tasks related to design and architectural processes. This palette offers a set of tools and options that enable users to create and manage wizard groups efficiently. It serves as a central point for users to select and operate different wizards tailored for specific tasks, thereby streamlining workflow and improving usability.

Structurally, the Wizards Palette presents frequently used tools in a pictogram-like format, which helps in quick identification and access. It is presented as an interactive component within Allplan's user interface, facilitating guided workflows and assisting users in navigating complex design processes. This feature also allows for user customization, enabling individuals to modify and organize wizard functionalities according to their preferences.

Overall, the Wizards Palette functions as a crucial interface element that empowers users to optimize their document creation processes by providing predefined and customizable options, making it an essential part of Allplan’s comprehensive toolset.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03833b31b2891d602b91a99573458723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb11ec0fcfe86b8f7442326222d5684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d71107f0a79ff7cc43c431cc90d16de0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7b3646c698bb267fd480306b6058059&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0443ff7054b61eb5d09a5b1d3ff8b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc81bbce7f6732d5f7cf3b0c3a9f19e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dfb51c08102b928e5de30c60482227e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11e6318ef637ac2118c770f1d07667b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a16e06df8dafb9e5fc7590880a115b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d972323d000973abecd5a28b1f3110f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbffcefc317d0a7ea08df02ff6f2536</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896877</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wizard Group">
      <data key="d0">Wizard Group</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Wizard Group is a collection of wizard files organized for easier access and use.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03833b31b2891d602b91a99573458723</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Unlock Angle Toggle">
      <data key="d0">Unlock Angle Toggle</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Unlock Angle Toggle is a feature related to angle adjustments in the context of design tools and software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-03833b31b2891d602b91a99573458723</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888394</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layers">
      <data key="d0">Layers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Layers are important organizational elements in design processes, particularly in Computer-Aided Design (CAD) systems, where they provide a structure for organizing data in projects. They are components within design software that can be visible or hidden, modified, and assigned specific properties, thus affecting how various features are applied and how components interact with one another.

In design environments, layers represent different levels or components that facilitate a structured hierarchy for managing objects. These layers allow for the manipulation of visibility settings and the sorting of graphical elements, contributing to orderly project organization and management. In CAD systems, layers enhance workflow by influencing project organization and providing advantages in managing concurrent design work, leading to increased productivity.

Specifically within software applications like Allplan, layers may possess unique settings or configurations that help users manage graphical elements effectively. They serve as crucial interfaces, enabling users to organize and control design components, enhancing overall management of drawing files.

In summary, layers are foundational to the architecture of design software, offering essential functionalities for organizing, managing, and accessing project data while supporting collaborative design efforts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5493e550e39dd75b531fbc279a9ede75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c9198643b99c59d271fc71c45c3c2ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e51e7bae74af0b0a490800f2339aec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8ac3d28483fa91b3321f28d53b3f3b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c0106e2517d0a358de436cfa49aa6d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8131350ef261324c331ea06679be0970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce679f4475fbeabc70afd38f6ec1209f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51ad59fa11ea060462215b76a065d23d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d1f1c3fcf05d1748919b120f4653f3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd4d53209a8c233eed20b711846b2af8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb38dce302a6fcd1fc4b9c0473f93438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ea5a3d45dc98ece1ae74ce8d2a84548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a36c3f2b433b78adbb71a8d05d151351&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-733ccd68ff0a99144a757b5b240bbf14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935cacdbf30f098651e73da157d12d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed89267b8149ebe7350a0b2c623d43bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-036f19dbc532c13244ce44b4a9245f4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7de4a9655cd1f8f5827eda34f82eaeb4</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896600</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CAD System">
      <data key="d0">CAD System</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A CAD system is a computer-aided design tool used for specialist design processes, facilitating project development with layers.&lt;SEP&gt;The CAD system refers to computer-aided design software used for design and engineering, with considerations for features like layering and organization in files.&lt;SEP&gt;A CAD system is a technology used for creating precise drawings and technical illustrations, facilitating design and collaborative work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5493e550e39dd75b531fbc279a9ede75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d698e6b659f48a57e6aa85d05abacf23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd4d53209a8c233eed20b711846b2af8</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896834</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Print Sets">
      <data key="d0">Print Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Print sets are user-defined compilations of layers that assist in editing and assembling layouts in design projects.&lt;SEP&gt;Print sets are collections of layers that can be selected for compiling and arranging layouts in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Print sets involve the configurations and specifications for printing outputs from the software, also relevant in the discussion of Allplan 2020.&lt;SEP&gt;Print sets are functionalities linked to controlling layer visibility and are essential for managing how information is presented in the application.&lt;SEP&gt;Print Sets dictate which layers are visible in layouts, essential for managing data in design.&lt;SEP&gt;Print Sets are settings within Allplan software that dictate how layers appear in printed documentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5493e550e39dd75b531fbc279a9ede75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db8e86f57de8392c5e7b235d611e395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed89267b8149ebe7350a0b2c623d43bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23b4d1b60a8c6ef686d0d35adaf060b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a2ed5fa5191731937d4da6939a4cb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca427f324dfe621e19edffc901a56dd</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896839</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DXF/DWG">
      <data key="d0">DXF/DWG</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">DXF/DWG are file formats used for data exchange in CAD, allowing layers to be organized and managed efficiently.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5493e550e39dd75b531fbc279a9ede75</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888395</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Current Layer">
      <data key="d0">Current Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The current layer is the layer that is actively being edited or modified within the Layers palette.&lt;SEP&gt;The current layer is the layer that is actively used for drawing elements, determined by the selection of tools in the CAD system.&lt;SEP&gt;Current Layer indicates the active layer on which drawing or modifications occur.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5493e550e39dd75b531fbc279a9ede75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec22abab62a86e389dc5d86bb0bf9c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a61ccb6676dd29927dd71994c7903dc</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896846</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Components">
      <data key="d0">Components</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Components refer to the design elements that can be organized within the layer structure in a CAD system.&lt;SEP&gt;Components is a labeled group within the Elements tab that contains tools used in the design and arrangement processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Components refer to the individual parts or modules within the software environment that contribute to its overall functionality and structure.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5493e550e39dd75b531fbc279a9ede75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e27c3e8ee5f8899b11e5218eec58459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14ec08840c3fa4e52e44aa4c6e2af111</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896829</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Special Button">
      <data key="d0">Special Button</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Special button in the CAD software allows for specifying whether openings can be assigned to independent layers.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5493e550e39dd75b531fbc279a9ede75</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888395</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Designer">
      <data key="d0">Designer</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Designers are individuals involved in creating and managing design projects, often working with layers and drawing files.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-5493e550e39dd75b531fbc279a9ede75</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888395</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Role">
      <data key="d0">Role</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Role in Allplan represents a specific set of tasks and responsibilities assigned to a user, affecting available tools and functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;A role defines a set of tools and functionalities assigned to a user within the Actionbar.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b532fa4a8ab92ded3fea1d57304eeffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888395</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Task Area">
      <data key="d0">Task Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Task Areas in Allplan are sections within the Actionbar that group related tools based on different design or modeling functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Task Area refers to sections in the Actionbar where tools are grouped by functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b532fa4a8ab92ded3fea1d57304eeffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888395</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Menu Bar">
      <data key="d0">Menu Bar</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Menu Bar in Allplan is a part of the user interface that provides access to various tools and options relevant to the user's current role and tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Menu Bar is a graphical interface component that includes options such as 'Create', 'Change', 'Repeat', and 'Window'.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b532fa4a8ab92ded3fea1d57304eeffd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e59d49f8f69534f63baf7c253ab95eeb</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896858</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Allplan Share">
      <data key="d0">Allplan Share</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Allplan Share is a feature in Allplan that allows users to upload and share project data, enhancing collaboration among users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b532fa4a8ab92ded3fea1d57304eeffd</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888395</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Viewport">
      <data key="d0">Viewport</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A viewport is a designated area within Allplan where design entities are displayed, allowing different views of the model.&lt;SEP&gt;A Viewport in Allplan refers to a specific area where the 3D model is displayed for viewing and interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Viewport refers to a section of the display in Allplan that allows users to view and interact with the design in different modes and perspectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Viewport is a concept discussed in relation to modeling environments, concerning functionality and arrangements for efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Viewport is a term used in software applications to describe a window or area for displaying content.&lt;SEP&gt;The viewport represents the area in the software interface where users can view and interact with their design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-712ac7e367720bf0768cb3b167957363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfac8b75410f9e9fa0a25fdb3d365c19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2e09e8bba60f1d58ef71be4e357ed2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0b79892ea245e6fed9c92748dc8298b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ccbbd757b5c34391eac2eed18afed86a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a238b21499e5951f5af21aafc0d71b8</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896705</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Perspective View">
      <data key="d0">Perspective View</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Perspective View is a type of visual representation in Allplan that provides depth and realism to the model.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888395</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Viewport Toolbar">
      <data key="d0">Viewport Toolbar</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Viewport Toolbar is a comprehensive toolset found at the bottom of each viewport in various design software applications, facilitating user interaction with viewport-related functions. It serves as a user interface feature that enhances the experience of viewing and manipulating 3D models, allowing users to access essential tools for navigation and management of design elements.

The Viewport Toolbar includes functionalities such as zooming and panning, helping users to restore previous views or adjust display scales efficiently. This collection of tools is integral to the design process, providing a streamlined method for users to manipulate their views or selections within a digital workspace. Although specific details about all the functions of the Viewport Toolbar may be lacking, it is undoubtedly a crucial component for viewport management in design applications, enabling effective interaction with the software's viewing features. 

In summary, the Viewport Toolbar encompasses various tools tailored to support users in navigating and controlling the visual aspects of their design work, ensuring a fluid and productive user experience.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2e09e8bba60f1d58ef71be4e357ed2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a74c3ed42cc5322cb0c4959773fc2ee5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7b89a901d889c8a225a5b773dea38a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59abaea139ed7c59a07634ff0e5d27f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f953bb379ef3c1fa82a44361051dd131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7aa2de35051a07440a4fda92b2ec401c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c46ec334a5537671d0130ddf1f37b6da</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896899</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Keyboard Shortcuts">
      <data key="d0">Keyboard Shortcuts</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Keyboard Shortcuts are predefined key combinations that serve to enhance user efficiency within the Allplan software. These shortcuts provide quick access to various functions, tools, and commands, significantly improving navigation and interaction across the software environment. They are designed to streamline workflows, allowing users to activate tools quickly and manipulate the 3D model or manage structural elements with greater ease.

In Allplan, keyboard shortcuts are integral to configurations that boost overall user experience. They not only aid in the efficient navigation of the software but also enhance actions related to perspective adjustments and data management. The application of keyboard shortcuts extends beyond just technical functionalities; they are critical for improving operational speed, especially in complex tasks such as managing and manipulating 3D environments.

Overall, keyboard shortcuts play a vital role in maximizing productivity for users of Allplan, making them an essential component for anyone aiming to work efficiently within design software, including functionalities used in ProjectPilot. This streamlined method of invoking commands contributes to a better, more effective user interaction with the installed program, underscoring the importance of mastering these key combinations for successful software utilization.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dc5b6b3a2775affb0d58bb05d664df8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1be1782cf19027851f94de5abece6998&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c36318c700d8e026eded8b42d35c63ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-612a0a7c6ba44b36c75a40ec9bbc3672&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cffbd9969b9035c99a670310a30d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08f8b5df1347cfcef0c4dd2547d03124&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c145032969306b2dc3113e1f39fcea29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3bf8515f342502ea30e1d362975d491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-886d493f4d1ef162aa3d5e7a25cd7147&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e495b0cd79cc88f595fa746df2e7844&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d084f8d91bd7ea701e82581899432ab3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b88363080af7a831ae295ad788a5e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7a6fb96d2c4d3280b5d585d719a7c55</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896734</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Render Methods">
      <data key="d0">Render Methods</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Render Methods are techniques in Allplan used to display models in different visual styles, such as Wireframe, Hidden, Shaded, or Sketch.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888395</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Setting">
      <data key="d0">Setting</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Setting refers to the configuration options within Allplan that affect how elements are displayed and interacted with on the screen.&lt;SEP&gt;Setting signifies an environment or configuration mentioned in relation to the viewport context, but not further elaborated.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fde471e05524fc7c6b4b31e21a3ad989</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896897</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Display Options">
      <data key="d0">Display Options</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Display Options are preferences within Allplan that determine how design elements appear on the screen, including visibility and formatting.&lt;SEP&gt;Display options refer to settings that allow users to change how elements are viewed within the viewport.&lt;SEP&gt;Display Options encompass settings or parameters that control how elements appear in design software, potentially including priorities for color and other visual attributes.&lt;SEP&gt;Display options relate to rules and settings for showing elements, which the discarded content fails to connect with.&lt;SEP&gt;Display options are user-defined settings that influence how graphical elements are rendered and their visibility in drawing software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e5ebfe23ff024ee5600dcd4f647debee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77ade8558cee074a5d462bd041c060e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b95a74a61bb3105e19ebfaa9ff3cfbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62485062fb13770bfe47cfd466509beb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b90194951b22f7e396d80356b767bd94</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896818</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
