    <node id="PDF Files">
      <data key="d0">PDF Files</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">PDF files are a format for saving and archiving print layouts that can be printed later.&lt;SEP&gt;PDF files are digital document formats relevant to printing tasks and mentioned in the context of exporting and creating layouts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e1b20c02cb1df7f4a3acfb70d457cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5dc0e7ea4aef9186abcaf494de198c9</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896823</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Color Option">
      <data key="d0">Color Option</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Color option refers to a setting that enables color printing on printers capable of producing color layouts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e1b20c02cb1df7f4a3acfb70d457cbf</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888396</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Export PDF Data Tool">
      <data key="d0">Export PDF Data Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Export PDF Data Tool allows users to save layouts as PDF files for later printing and archiving.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-0e1b20c02cb1df7f4a3acfb70d457cbf</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888396</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tool">
      <data key="d0">Tool</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A tool is an implementation within the Actionbar used for performing specific operations or tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;A tool is a specific feature or option available in the software, often accessible via a shortcut menu for creating or editing elements.&lt;SEP&gt;The term 'Tool' is implied by the character '器' and refers to devices or implements used in 3D modeling and other functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Tool refers to different functionalities available for drawing lines as described in the table.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dfd61e93c0a8c944e4ce3d2c31edf67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4053b391a6a6cb6d07e5301f59184d0b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896698</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Flyout Menu">
      <data key="d0">Flyout Menu</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Flyout Menu is a dropdown menu showing similar tools when a primary tool is selected.&lt;SEP&gt;The flyout menu, associated with the Modeling tab, provides additional tool options that are visually highlighted in the interface.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e6b80e48bef3738c39a27291a07173f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896838</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Customize User Interface">
      <data key="d0">Customize User Interface</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The method to configure the Actionbar and adjust tool visibility in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Customize User Interface refers to the settings and options available in Allplan that allow users to modify the appearance and behavior of the software to better fit their needs.&lt;SEP&gt;Customize User Interface refers to the process of adjusting software settings to improve user experience and productivity within the software environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Customize User Interface is an option in the Vertical Menu suggesting functionalities for tailoring the user experience in the software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1729b2d3689ebe861c41881a390fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05575fdf899295156f6bf0490548a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2682cda91fcc66490a3823382618a08a</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Actionbar Configurator">
      <data key="d0">Actionbar Configurator</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Actionbar Configurator is a feature in Allplan that allows users to customize the Actionbar and manage roles.&lt;SEP&gt;The Actionbar Configurator is a tool related to the Actionbar that allows for customization and configuration of features.&lt;SEP&gt;The Actionbar Configurator refers to a set of features and configuration processes associated with managing the Actionbar in software applications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Actionbar Configurator is a software tool mentioned in the context of customization capabilities and advanced configuration tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The Actionbar Configurator is a tool that allows users to tailor the Actionbar functionality to their preferences within Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Actionbar Configurator is a tool within Allplan software that allows users to configure and customize the Actionbar.&lt;SEP&gt;The Actionbar Configurator is a tool associated with Allplan, aimed at user interface customization and management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10c213bf3e73dbb3668162f050af15d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a05e93f0e688a92715cf960bc9488f6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44b9fe086a75a98f106bad351c259ab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ead411bc27ddadc770622c6d9da2f37c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0e957393684b272e0278e8a908a2f09&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d65497005b60327e29c7038a77e2a503</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896805</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Configuration File">
      <data key="d0">Configuration File</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A Configuration File stores settings and roles for the Actionbar in Allplan, saved as .actb.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888396</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Import Roles Area">
      <data key="d0">Import Roles Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Import Roles Area shows imported roles in Actionbar Configurator before they are assigned to the user interface.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888396</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Properties Palette">
      <data key="d0">Properties Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Properties Palette is a crucial tool within the Allplan software, designed for displaying and modifying the properties of selected elements in a drawing. This user interface element facilitates adjustments to various design attributes, including pen thickness, line type, and line color, allowing users to customize their drawings according to their specific needs.

The Properties Palette plays a significant role in managing the settings related to selected objects or components within a project. It provides a comprehensive interface that reflects user preferences and configurations, enhancing the overall user experience. Users can access a range of functionalities through this palette, which includes options for customizing workspace arrangements and accessing keyboard shortcuts.

Considered a vital component of Allplan's CAD program, the Properties Palette not only displays object attributes but also allows users to adjust various settings and functionalities related to their selected items. It operates as a floating palette that contributes significantly to user interaction with the software, integrating various display and modification capabilities that streamline the design process.

Overall, the Properties Palette serves as an essential feature within Allplan, enabling effective management of design elements and enhancing the productivity of users by offering readily adjustable settings tailored to their design projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a6145ea75d080e54922523c67fac964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c5287c4c8d2cc121dff7af4c8f5b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abb11ec0fcfe86b8f7442326222d5684&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f6d6c0fc9029b0a0cac77b61d25be98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1729b2d3689ebe861c41881a390fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05575fdf899295156f6bf0490548a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b7a1518e12c82ed346ccdcd608eaf52e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032462a24ce269c64a42e612a0c5a765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8f11c6e348e0368cafc8a5e36275c9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1aece73f9e99cbab085a302da350f44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90ba399bd36c92c0abddb5d44bedb3e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b0bb15ab024dcd0058d974e339078c5</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896872</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Library Palette">
      <data key="d0">Library Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Library Palette is used to manage symbols, smart symbols, SmartParts, and PythonParts for design purposes in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Palette is a tool within Allplan for managing and retrieving design symbols and components.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Palette is a feature in Allplan that allows users to access and manage stored symbols, including smart symbols, for use in a project.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Palette is another specific palette type, associated with functionalities for organizing and accessing resources within the software.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Palette is a user interface component within software that provides access to library elements for enhanced user interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Palette is a feature of Allplan Software that may have been referenced in the discarded content for tips or instructions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Library Palette is a section of the Allplan software interface displaying various design elements, including chair thumbnails.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf93c97b7398da09d1cabc644a3e194&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d305d677976b85ecf574260a9460d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc81bbce7f6732d5f7cf3b0c3a9f19e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11e6318ef637ac2118c770f1d07667b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc8fd449cd88e5b4bff938d487714ce2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3011bf331b8ccd9c11164ec5fa962211</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896873</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Objects Palette">
      <data key="d0">Objects Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Objects Palette is a tool within Allplan, a comprehensive design software that facilitates the management of objects in drawing files. It provides users with functionalities that allow for sorting, organizing, and controlling the visibility of various design elements. The Objects Palette lists all objects currently available in the open drawing files, enabling quick access and adjustments to these items.

In addition to sorting and visibility controls, the Objects Palette serves as a collection of pre-defined elements that users can easily insert into their designs, streamlining the creation process. It enhances navigation and efficiency within the design interface by incorporating specific functionalities tailored for managing graphical elements. The palette includes control features that allow users to manipulate object attributes such as transparency and overall visibility, ensuring that design processes are both effective and user-friendly.

Furthermore, the Objects Palette is integral to interacting with library elements within the software, although details on specific functionalities may vary. This makes it not only a tool for aesthetic adjustments but also a vital component for organizing complex design tasks. It is a feature designed to optimize users' experience in a graphical interface, focusing on object management within the Allplan environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f12df672618de36e5be89afed9ceb5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a007e42b9b683c4bb5c145f80014d5b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1729b2d3689ebe861c41881a390fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-61c80c48e779ad023af2379778b857d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827e971c3e5ed16f366a1af31ae5d816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9431f19cca4d71b3534c26b00fde366f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5693db3b9df92346f1abf7e3e49409a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7371c601a5243c554f050195081be62b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc8d88526e9108bd7399a03dfe87aff8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8aae6be41afa02c7491334a34fd8144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45133550f2868ebabb97ae48210fee25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4214a7ad25394b1516ea471827743477&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eee637b59b6ed6c157aae67c5875def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c80cee8413b50a66012329408f970f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5b72be4d941b99db4f3a965779be38f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b050584edb1451b0b32e7a849e336a91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdce630877092efc4b68b70b07c7a1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3483e846d3a461436f2e30d70ffcc1c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4adb555ec296181c94ed6a874a44ef19&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7578ecb7eb533e1c12df0b6c3289aebd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a653d4534e4d996656ae034933b2ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32ec456ee3071a7e66f63071db4d4f76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71cdd6b856e230d3c1c50860bf2874f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20b4f548da1efdcf42769f24b82626cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c977c201478b50e405ef853ddf1f81c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896759</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Planes Palette">
      <data key="d0">Planes Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Planes Palette is a significant feature within the Allplan software, primarily designed for managing and editing plane models related to current building structures. This component plays a crucial role in architectural design, allowing users to check, modify, and create plane models that are integral to the overall representation of the building.

In Allplan, the Planes Palette provides functionalities that enable users to interact with various elements of the modeling environment. It includes tools for rendering materials, managing object properties, and executing operational procedures related to the manipulation of these models. Key features of the Planes Palette encompass the ability to expand, collapse, and update models, along with inserting different types of planes and adjusting model attributes.

The Planes Palette is prominently discussed in the software manual, where it is characterized as a comprehensive toolkit for architectural modeling. Within this context, it supports various operational capabilities that enhance user interaction with design elements. Furthermore, it is recognized as an essential part of the user interface, offering toolbar functionalities that streamline the modeling process.

Overall, the Planes Palette serves as a versatile tool within Allplan that facilitates effective architectural design through its robust features for managing and customizing plane models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1729b2d3689ebe861c41881a390fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e3b4f81956c29be44ec682974281e07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc8059cdd03fac1892599a1246a1caf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2a653d4534e4d996656ae034933b2ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1986c44593e743c0fbc014601da43fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5201dfdc74ffefb5afea6252e9430709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f22c5e3620a1555c869882ed19098c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-518e5828dc41e29c9c94dd71ab66b03e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50551537a5ed73cb4bb218fdea45e3fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08fe6ca99f223dbf5e299c05b6a2af7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a2bff0956001a90e38664cf455131ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-045789d54d9c59dfae128c442d815e63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2018a3aee91e2763c1853d692049064&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e07a0897553b878f83490a95d033991d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-677a7ccd7efeefbbedde3003158a7bbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4523e049fc00468e44d53f5c090def24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-766e9d42e579b657017314ab5c6c26e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0f981c43c05a510118a9858f8fe6597</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896778</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Task Board Palette">
      <data key="d0">Task Board Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Task Board Palette in Allplan facilitates the management and editing of tasks within Bimplus projects.&lt;SEP&gt;The Task Board Palette enables users to check and edit the tasks of Bimplus projects directly within Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Task Board Palette facilitates communication and task management in a Bimplus project within the Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;The Task Board palette is a feature within Allplan software used for managing entries and tasks in a plane model.&lt;SEP&gt;The Task Board Palette is a tool referenced in the context of user interactions with Allplan, highlighting its importance in modifying models and saving settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bc2e5e1cca4bececa7176b1cd5853d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b91a6868a9646c017d41c0d935b68c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1729b2d3689ebe861c41881a390fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b864b99322a1987666544438aeb6e82a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a893d16b0a9cdad9f06bff3dc372a370</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896785</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Wizards">
      <data key="d0">Wizards</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Wizards are interactive tools within software applications, particularly in the context of Allplan, designed to assist users in performing specific tasks effectively and efficiently. They provide guided user interactions, making complex functionalities more accessible through a step-by-step process or predefined options. These tools play a crucial role in enhancing the user experience by simplifying processes such as setup, configuration, and editing tasks.

Within the Allplan software, Wizards serve as customizable elements that help users navigate various features, including saving and grouping functionalities. They are integral to the user interface, allowing individuals to modify and edit elements with ease. Furthermore, Wizards are categorized as features that can either be predefined or customizable, aiding in the automation of repetitive tasks and supporting more efficient workflows.

In summary, Wizards in Allplan function as essential aids that facilitate user interactions with the software, promoting simplicity and effectiveness in task execution across diverse applications within the software environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd46724bce30a7f59584e419db1f9ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0443ff7054b61eb5d09a5b1d3ff8b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a11034421bff5eb8de0b9e4403a5ea9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-363665dee7592ae64c945b922f8baaa8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b671bba7089145f32ec4ba1a3653bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab667139b917a372bb8a62cedd891e8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54fc5161861531710c469a7ee8a1f087&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fef85cc503c935dbcc7499f77c30f37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cafbc27f0be77894cf80b881467df55e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e648adbf0bea41bc274839d25095aa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfce13511997571e0bc691490b6e5f1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8681a5ebe1155a5dca8d56eb646e25db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c6b1e47ccd8e9b3f6cace8ca796bc49&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2682cda91fcc66490a3823382618a08a</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896876</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Element">
      <data key="d0">Element</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Element refers to the individual components or objects that can be selected and manipulated within a drawing or graphical environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Element refers to objects in design, including lines, hatching, and symbols.&lt;SEP&gt;An element refers to a specific object or item in the software that can be manipulated using various tools and wizards.&lt;SEP&gt;Element refers to a fundamental component within a software interface related to design or architectural projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d202d87f74ec6d653a0d9a932427c930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a7f0767ef25d5ccf08b2066d8717659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a789f6f9ddfb3c5b68ed9d65b75d54e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896870</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Input Options">
      <data key="d0">Input Options</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Input Options encompass a range of settings and functionalities that control how input tools behave within software, particularly in the context of design applications like Allplan. This section introduces various methodologies available for users to interact with the software effectively during the creation of elements or areas.

The Input Options are specifically relevant to user interactions, detailing the available input methods that enhance the usability of the design software. This includes the different ways users can specify data when working on design elements such as polylines and areas. The options dictate how tools, particularly those for entering polylines, function. Users can select among various configurations to tailor their interaction, which directly affects how they work with the software.

In Allplan, Input Options play a critical role by providing settings related to mouse usage and other input methodologies. These settings inform users about the selections they can make when creating polylines, ultimately aiming to optimize their design experience and interaction with the software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e2ed9fe3dbf8e53206649b8a3c53c683&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-005d6e213ff60df2f8e1b0d009ada5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f67ba39d262d631a03b828eff1df523a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ceccfc99bb5d38a3c7818f80749f93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-50e9df5a650fbc684ffb520e8dadb5ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f4f6cb906fc59cc7901b866dc3aa70e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-096c93d4475023fc3548c92aa1d260b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60900cf1962b337160c2cfe9ddfe6e4</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896738</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Polyline Entry Tools">
      <data key="d0">Polyline Entry Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Polyline Entry Tools are features in the software that allow users to create polylines and polygonal areas for design purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyline entry tools are functionalities that allow users to create and manipulate polylines effectively in CAD software.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyline entry tools are functionalities discussed in the surrounding content that involve specific operational details necessary for accurate usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyline entry tools are features within Allplan that allow users to create shapes through point selection and form polylines.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyline entry tools are functionalities used in architectural drafting software to create and manage polylines effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyline entry tools are features in architectural CAD software used for inputting polylines and detecting areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Polyline entry tools are features in digital design applications that assist users in creating and managing polylines and areas in architectural drawings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a27839fe34b8ded0988268a250aab5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df09f608c1b8cff3375bf406d718e78c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e47cada67781b120785f4128f163bc2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f5ea9513f17ec52fcf59f7e156d0af0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e60900cf1962b337160c2cfe9ddfe6e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3635cb058949af2a97c6e77f4de7d81d</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896753</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Polygonization">
      <data key="d0">Polygonization</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Polygonization is a process that involves converting various design elements into polygon shapes, which is essential in architectural design and modeling software. This functionality is notably significant in software like Allplan, where polygonization supports the creation, management, and manipulation of geometric areas using polygons. It plays a critical role in workflows by allowing users to convert polylines into polygons, thereby facilitating area detection, defining boundaries, and rendering shapes accurately.

In particular, polygonization is utilized for approximating curves and outlining segments, enhancing the precision needed in architectural models. It serves both as a technique for converting existing shapes into polygons and as a method to structure defined areas effectively within design interfaces. Furthermore, polygonization is not only relevant for drawing software but is also integral to mathematical modeling, as it assists in area evaluations and the manipulation of design elements. The process is essential for ensuring that designs can be accurately represented and effectively worked with in various architectural applications. 

Overall, polygonization stands out as a foundational aspect of the design process in architecture, impacting both the visual and functional aspects of modeling within software environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df09f608c1b8cff3375bf406d718e78c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98fa1fd4f191a1441ffaf749a1d57a54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c0ae73519022616e415d7ef1d192a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655a4c80e2acaf8c6e89b896c12a2dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9f8c8fd2d057097074e5781243bb5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f2f16a99d8ed5edf18e8f8fefa073c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c885d9129226949857a102f86514e827&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa5f19da184966b9597323c17e4c8365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebdb2951ad2bbbb60ea48469cd679ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3619640ff74d418328624e5335130ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-543b00f9d3bc0de82a9c61d23b8586d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7460ea58ee99d764421fc3d9f144da87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be94afa5c2a76739d14a8fc311413f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0190fcbe0c8e4dd19ee576c6cae8a094</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896763</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Area Detection">
      <data key="d0">Area Detection</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Area Detection is a multifaceted feature prominently utilized within design software, particularly in Allplan. This functionality allows users to automatically detect and outline closed polygons based on user-defined criteria, making it essential for accurate architectural modeling and design. The process involves identifying specific areas within a defined space and often employs additional points to refine the precision of area measurements.

As a critical aspect of computer-aided design (CAD), Area Detection serves various purposes, such as helping to determine and measure areas within designs. This includes identifying and managing spaces within geometric shapes and applying surface elements effectively. The area detection feature is integral to the broader functionality of Allplan, facilitating polygon creation and the identification of curve outlines, enabling users to navigate design complexities with greater ease.

Moreover, Area Detection plays a significant role in architectural design, as it is geared towards determining physical or mathematical regions within design elements. Various techniques employed facilitate the identification of these areas, ensuring that project plans are executed with meticulous attention to spatial dimensions, which is crucial for precision in architectural and design contexts.

The methodology surrounding Area Detection encompasses several approaches, including polygonization techniques that aid in area identification and management, particularly in projects necessitating an understanding of geometric precision. Overall, Area Detection ensures that architects and designers can efficiently outline and calculate areas within specific boundaries, leveraging this feature to enhance the functionality and accuracy of their design work.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00307343bc370b11443bafa835be22b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4152424e127dd305bed7dcaa03e8d422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5680123964cab6893360eca2fbdbe91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df09f608c1b8cff3375bf406d718e78c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98fa1fd4f191a1441ffaf749a1d57a54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-881a0db0a5fa23fc88efcf480aeb7ac2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8c0ae73519022616e415d7ef1d192a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-655a4c80e2acaf8c6e89b896c12a2dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58123899844bda31e27d8c11086052e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d9f8c8fd2d057097074e5781243bb5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f2f16a99d8ed5edf18e8f8fefa073c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e00c09e03bfb6f7b7d1520b2a600e03b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa5f19da184966b9597323c17e4c8365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52a6beb36885923713b1405d5c329d66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ebdb2951ad2bbbb60ea48469cd679ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7460ea58ee99d764421fc3d9f144da87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f19fc9049a6665b44293bf478d8b865&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5be94afa5c2a76739d14a8fc311413f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1979ba0f8d29d8d9c47edf9e866d128&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef654b1e3ef63a37895f103aab89d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7508773c6f055dacc49fabc771f103bf</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896759</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Island Detection">
      <data key="d0">Island Detection</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Island Detection is a tool used to identify and manage closed outlines within a design area, allowing for adjustments to be made to the overall area.&lt;SEP&gt;Island Detection is a method used to detect closed outlines within an area and automatically cut them out.&lt;SEP&gt;Island detection is a specific polygonization technique that focuses on recognizing isolated areas within a design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-adcf04405d5dc9edd7324bbd5ad01339&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00307343bc370b11443bafa835be22b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58123899844bda31e27d8c11086052e0</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896760</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Object Navigator">
      <data key="d0">Object Navigator</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Object Navigator is a feature in Allplan that allows users to manage object visibility and sorting within the software.&lt;SEP&gt;The Object Navigator is an interface feature in Allplan that helps users manage and interact with model elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc8059cdd03fac1892599a1246a1caf</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896775</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Modification Mode">
      <data key="d0">Modification Mode</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Modification Mode is a setting in Allplan that allows users to see and modify plane models across all viewports.&lt;SEP&gt;Modification Mode is an operational state allowing users to change height settings of planes and reference surfaces.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b91a6868a9646c017d41c0d935b68c7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Selection Button">
      <data key="d0">Selection Button</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Selection Button is used in Allplan to toggle between visible/invisible and active/inactive object states.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Insert Pair of Planes">
      <data key="d0">Insert Pair of Planes</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Insert Pair of Planes is a function in Allplan that allows users to insert pairs of planes into the current plane model.&lt;SEP&gt;Insert Pair of Planes is a command within the Planes Palette that allows users to manipulate elements of plane models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08fe6ca99f223dbf5e299c05b6a2af7b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896778</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Custom Sorting">
      <data key="d0">Custom Sorting</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Custom Sorting refers to a feature that allows users to define sorting criteria for organizing objects in the Objects Palette.&lt;SEP&gt;Custom Sorting is a feature in Allplan that enables users to sort objects based on user-defined criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Floor Manager">
      <data key="d0">Floor Manager</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Floor Manager is a dialog box in Allplan that allows users to manage and insert default planes and other structural elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Floor Manager is a method mentioned for creating building structures, which likely involves managing different levels of a building.&lt;SEP&gt;Floor Manager is a software program featuring a user interface designed for managing building layouts and their hierarchical structures.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdea26b8c5364ac43c1e1ce6ec4898e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fbec976e832c12ede39ca9e557fea65</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896731</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Roofscape">
      <data key="d0">Roofscape</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Roofscape refers to the configuration and appearance of roof structures in architectural modeling, which can be inserted or replaced in plane models.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Offset Plane">
      <data key="d0">Offset Plane</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">An Offset Plane is a plane in Allplan that is linked to a default plane at a specific offset, adapting automatically to changes in the linked plane.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-e271b0bc80906c67904b47ed0ad95172</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Office Administrator">
      <data key="d0">Office Administrator</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">The office administrator is responsible for managing layers and layer structures and defining privilege sets.&lt;SEP&gt;The Office Administrator is responsible for managing layer access rights and overseeing layer management practices.&lt;SEP&gt;The Office Administrator is responsible for managing layers and creating project-specific layer structures within the design software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4668db98dab082ae62dab9476dd1460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-876fb7c4401ed46b5aac412e596a87f3</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896846</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Privilege Sets">
      <data key="d0">Privilege Sets</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Privilege sets control user access to layers and can be assigned based on project roles.&lt;SEP&gt;Privilege sets pertain to user permissions and restrictions within the software, relevant to the functionalities encompassing Allplan 2020.&lt;SEP&gt;Privilege sets are functionalities that control layer visibility within the application, integral for user permissions and access management.&lt;SEP&gt;Privilege Sets are defined as components that control access to layers in digital design environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Privilege Sets are settings in Allplan software that determine user permissions related to layer visibility and access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db8e86f57de8392c5e7b235d611e395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed89267b8149ebe7350a0b2c623d43bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23b4d1b60a8c6ef686d0d35adaf060b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a2ed5fa5191731937d4da6939a4cb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ca427f324dfe621e19edffc901a56dd</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896839</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layer Dialog Box">
      <data key="d0">Layer Dialog Box</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Layer Dialog Box is a user interface component primarily utilized in Allplan software for managing layer administration tasks in architectural drawing projects. This tool allows users to manage layers by showing, hiding, and modifying them, thereby playing a crucial role in the organization and visibility of project elements.

In addition to its basic functionalities, the Layer Dialog Box also serves as an interface within ProjectPilot, where it is used to define format properties based on project layers. This dual functionality highlights the importance of the Layer Dialog Box across different aspects of project management in architectural software.

The Layer Dialog Box is recognized as essential for establishing project specifications, often featuring dropdown menus and tabs that enhance the user experience by providing comprehensive instructions related to layer management. This interface is designed to accommodate advanced functionalities, allowing users to efficiently navigate and utilize its features for effective project outcomes. 

Overall, the Layer Dialog Box in Allplan software is integral for architectural layer management, facilitating user interaction and enhancing productivity through its comprehensive set of tools and features.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef853aad5cd628db1d2c34ebbb5835e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81cf5c85be9f4469f5b46f9f3d23dc66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7098321c2776e7e778c6bbb3c1ca42a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17c478a3a7a4228b68608609441cc6e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4135e5fd8b98b66b5a6b0da1dfdb4cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3cc1f914a850b6c5593ff6fa507c8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f1a01e4dbcd714a2866b709318367c2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896637</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Workgroup Manager">
      <data key="d0">Workgroup Manager</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Workgroup Manager is a function within Allplan that allows for collaboration in a network environment, requiring administrator privileges for certain settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Workgroup manager is a feature in Allplan that facilitates user access management for collaborative projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Users">
      <data key="d0">Users</data>
      <data key="d1">person</data>
      <data key="d2">Users in a project can include architects, engineers, and other stakeholders who interact with layers and privilege sets.&lt;SEP&gt;Users are individuals seeking guidance on the setup and initial usage of Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;Users are individuals who may seek to understand the installation processes but lack prior knowledge due to the gaps in the discarded content.&lt;SEP&gt;Users are individuals who interact with Allplan and require guidance on installation steps for optimal usage.&lt;SEP&gt;Users of Allplan software seek to utilize the functionality and settings introduced in surrounding text for effective area management.&lt;SEP&gt;Users are individuals utilizing Allplan software who need to understand drawing file statuses for efficient workflow management.&lt;SEP&gt;Users are individuals who would benefit from the knowledge provided in the Installation, Basics content for effective software implementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1820b0451b7572f068cd0be91559b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d6279507e0ba43c05fee0ccf2016c14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ceccfc99bb5d38a3c7818f80749f93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cffbd9969b9035c99a670310a30d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20619f396aa0880142ac06d90643da2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18f8a7d980c71c0822b5e4c03ea409e7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896718</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Construction Layers">
      <data key="d0">Construction Layers</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Construction layers refer to the multiple layers that can exist within walls or upstands, each with different format properties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Properties Dialog Box">
      <data key="d0">Properties Dialog Box</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Properties dialog box is used to define the layer for each of the construction layers in a wall or upstand in Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1eb1a7d23a288b7df08a1ec6e85eb6bd</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Library Elements">
      <data key="d0">Library Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Library Elements refer to various components and features within library management systems and software applications that assist users in organizing, categorizing, and managing resources. These elements include symbols, SmartParts, PythonParts, and other reusable assets that can be selected, filtered, sorted, and visualized according to user preferences. They play a critical role in enhancing user productivity by providing an interface for interacting with the library’s content.

In the context of software applications like Allplan, Library Elements are specifically designed to aid users in navigating the user interface efficiently. They can be managed through palettes and include functionalities such as sorting and preview options. The elements are integral to the software, providing foundational knowledge for users in terms of how to manipulate and utilize the various resources available within the library.

Overall, Library Elements serve to streamline the design process within architectural programs by offering essential tools and menus that enhance the user experience. The emphasis on their organization and manipulation highlights their importance in maximizing the effectiveness of library systems, thereby contributing significantly to workflow efficiency and resource retrieval for users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12df672618de36e5be89afed9ceb5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6795482f136cc5e74fbfe680970a8a95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd4f98001bcdfeee78fe603290a396e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92133cc3204e73ae60da3b5bc728472d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c36f3a63b25adac0f2f1c1823bd09b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d72ad75c50fc8a5c04103f6b81e97b9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2116ea7560932e0de0e5b51b9fe5bb90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-042869791aa7bc0bef8bb8dd20ed4f0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a1422df29cf97e37272436bdcb85aa9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc34a20b1511a5b48efc030c747bb65a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd0f2e5447f7273835565e980268535&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dbe318ab0bed042490a3b6ddc033f85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32d42a5eabe03f05462c39f760738d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef06de7e10a2aa7e4cdbc38635d7cd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac49db71a2ded8e172c4d75eff9e32af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f58e24d8a483d7f261c4371c5734f0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0bd72ba56dc69681339b2d59b129ae</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896759</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Nemetschek Profile Catalog">
      <data key="d0">Nemetschek Profile Catalog</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Nemetschek Profile Catalog is a resource in Bimplus, enabling users to add profiles as symbols to the Allplan library.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nemetschek Profile Catalog provides a collection of design profiles for use within Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Nemetschek Profile Catalog is a library used in Allplan to store and manage various symbol profiles including smart symbols.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12df672618de36e5be89afed9ceb5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf93c97b7398da09d1cabc644a3e194&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d305d677976b85ecf574260a9460d5b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888397</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Symbols">
      <data key="d0">Symbols</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Symbols are visual representations used within design software, particularly in the context of Allplan. They serve multiple purposes, acting as graphical elements that can be selected, managed, and reused by users in technical drawings and designs. These symbols enhance usability by providing visual cues that indicate functionality when the cursor is positioned at key points in the drawing software, thus facilitating user interaction.

In Allplan, symbols are integral to the design workflow as they allow for predefined and reusable components, thereby promoting efficiency in design processes. Each symbol is defined with specific functionalities that aid in organizing user preferences and streamlining design tasks. The use of symbols helps to improve overall design efficiency by enabling designers to represent various elements graphically, contributing significantly to the design workflow within the software environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12df672618de36e5be89afed9ceb5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a93e1740be0b90b51787be4cb4fb06e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a44337414cf41fb33549c0a8097a841&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c363ac1543df296a0116c60c083334&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f93dfe57c8fc90fa6d294b523bed3995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8adfc2a8ed692a488fd180b2300080bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80384e61c69b8525123bddfac6a7f806&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a4cf5f011c03d3f7d318f9499a6edd6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60ed739e34b8ee76c942aff4971bffbb</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896789</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Smart Symbols">
      <data key="d0">Smart Symbols</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Smart Symbols are advanced functional elements in Allplan, a software used for modeling that aims to improve drawing efficiency. They represent a specific type of library element that can adapt to various design contexts, thus enhancing the overall usability of the software.

These intelligent symbols possess dynamic characteristics, allowing their appearance to change based on the reference scale and view. This includes features such as multiple display foils, which enable detailed or schematic representations of objects within the design environment. Smart Symbols function as advanced graphical elements that users can manipulate efficiently, thereby streamlining the design process.

In addition to serving as versatile design tools, Smart Symbols provide significant functionalities, especially in managing openings and room finish surfaces, thus facilitating user interaction and understanding in technical drafting. They are particularly noted for enhancing the user interface, although some descriptions noted a lack of specific contextual details in certain references.

Smart Symbols also contribute to flexible design practices, where their adaptability allows for modifications and custom definitions in diverse design settings. Ultimately, they represent a critical advancement within the Allplan software, characterized by their ability to enhance efficiency and support sophisticated design management through the use of libraries and defaults.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12df672618de36e5be89afed9ceb5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-722696e14943f4546267ecafc68e9e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d305d677976b85ecf574260a9460d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8adfc2a8ed692a488fd180b2300080bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ffbe3074d6dd43fef809fffc07d3094&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1cf8a9568a245cb114510ae01fd556d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca6dfc54cc34be7df573bffd25060a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-031abc09fbd44b3ece31b6449c940604&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6712dbbeb494f7b184f2716b64785e3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2be476b4c50c0ded1655c03aa85ca153&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcab7bf36d42e74a9733b00a931b4332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-354b91734a00cd848031c8604d1aeb47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8524dbb82a9bd657dac0d25e0f5e6674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22039614d79c8c7932c49ed4d1b694b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76cb544eec8c2890bdf1f96c8e3d8b50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5da781b1996f4a511381d9238dc01703&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28b00239e6c303f3dbbf28999b106a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-873d50beb4c644f62d830a0fe46147de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dec9e6bac8399e2cdc87edf066b216e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aec422f168f62147141326f0ddadc1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83af65e12ee702ab262db0503136673c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-329f92cc2da36955ab38253f01cebd3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e859227b6281968bb7a9aa4444e0a8ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94949a11445d74650a452d0168521a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b671bba7089145f32ec4ba1a3653bbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512f01abede97e6fdf1544a5c12dd614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a65488147c61ff601230e712beb997e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab331f7587826fc2f982efa84c7252e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f48d3394fec9db866021423f69f395c9</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896836</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="PythonParts">
      <data key="d0">PythonParts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">PythonParts are programmable components integrated within the Allplan software, designed to enhance customization and functionality in architectural modeling. They serve as scripting elements that allow for tailored object placement and innovative design solutions, thereby streamlining project designs and improving workflow efficiency.

As a specific type of parametric object, PythonParts are built on the Python programming language, which enables advanced automation and customization capabilities within the Allplan environment. These components are an integral part of SmartPart technology, adding vital functionalities that contribute to the overall effectiveness of architectural modeling processes. PythonParts not only facilitate enhanced design workflows but also require an understanding of installation and proper usage for optimal operation.

In the context of Allplan documentation, PythonParts is a significant topic, emphasizing their relevance as tools for creating parametric objects. While information on their exact functionalities within visual scripting in Allplan is sparse, it is clear that they contribute crucially to design customization and productivity enhancements, providing users with additional parametric modeling tools that expand the software's capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12df672618de36e5be89afed9ceb5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-722696e14943f4546267ecafc68e9e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7381ee705a6c05c03181833c355e759f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-658173db77812e1f794d53cc8ac5e2cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff0fa80147bc0d6ee30c8d17c03f9202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68ca69aea104d64cfe76c4f205fa5389&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1882718b5869bbabe6f97218372c273&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dba930ec8fd4bf4cabb39d5422013594&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d2be191399ff7925fc46310debdb78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76136ca392287606e69df79944c592c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52be88446c95f65fcc123514b345a6e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54141470321b9cf8611ae22bd386ca25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4034b1566017cc79f73d3679724b10d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94949a11445d74650a452d0168521a9</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896851</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="SmartParts">
      <data key="d0">SmartParts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">SmartParts is a sophisticated feature within the Allplan CAD software designed to enhance architectural design and modeling capabilities. These advanced library elements function as intelligent and parametric objects that allow users to create, insert, and modify complex geometries and design elements efficiently using predefined parameters. Importantly, SmartParts are saved into the user's workspace, enabling customized component creation tailored to specific project requirements.

SmartParts work independently and can be grouped, joined, sliced, or subtracted, which allows for versatile modeling options that meet intricate design needs. They play a crucial role in parametric CAD modeling, providing comprehensive functionalities and assisting with the integration of smart symbols to streamline modeling workflows. Consequently, SmartParts enhance the overall productivity and efficiency of architectural design processes by fostering effective task execution.

In addition to their core functionalities, SmartParts are also discussed in the context of technical instructions and collaborative features. By understanding installation and setup requirements, users can leverage these customizable tools more effectively. SmartParts serve as a foundational object type that lays the groundwork for even more advanced components, such as PythonParts, further expanding their capabilities within the Allplan environment.

Overall, SmartParts represent a critical component in modern architectural design, enriching the design process through customizable elements that improve both the design experience and outcome.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f12df672618de36e5be89afed9ceb5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d305d677976b85ecf574260a9460d5b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7381ee705a6c05c03181833c355e759f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28b00239e6c303f3dbbf28999b106a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dec9e6bac8399e2cdc87edf066b216e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aec422f168f62147141326f0ddadc1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-329f92cc2da36955ab38253f01cebd3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e859227b6281968bb7a9aa4444e0a8ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e7ca8ceb691ae838798710b4e164211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a1878040a560dfbd967a592f92ab0c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f31ea09b272bd98fc2266a66871c6d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85979115d94841259eb7c20933bb973d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9762338dd14cff37c047fc4aa2a65348&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82031cc2cd63e0794d3dcd00e43cdd89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f7189ab39e15329cd5659b8c899ae1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b28ef6ca46874e64effe1d160c93f4d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb5cc0338dd8e6019ef54f83163e0855&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a8a2d700391d265e9403dc2fefc41f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f17e24ec54f0bfb576495ae8c93f8508&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-569914f2ffbe0cafc272959ff5b72970&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-658173db77812e1f794d53cc8ac5e2cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff0fa80147bc0d6ee30c8d17c03f9202&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1882718b5869bbabe6f97218372c273&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dba930ec8fd4bf4cabb39d5422013594&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76136ca392287606e69df79944c592c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94949a11445d74650a452d0168521a9</data>
