    <node id="Search Results Folder">
      <data key="d0">Search Results Folder</data>
      <data key="d1">folder</data>
      <data key="d2">The Search Results folder is a temporary folder that displays found objects in ProjectPilot after a search operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef853aad5cd628db1d2c34ebbb5835e3</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888400</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Document Window">
      <data key="d0">Document Window</data>
      <data key="d1">interface</data>
      <data key="d2">The Document Window displays the contents of selected folders and projects in ProjectPilot, facilitating user interactions with files.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef853aad5cd628db1d2c34ebbb5835e3</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888400</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Folder">
      <data key="d0">Folder</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A Folder in ProjectPilot organizes projects and documents in a tree structure for user navigation and management.&lt;SEP&gt;A Folder is a directory structure used to organize files within the BIM software environment, showing the hierarchy of data storage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef853aad5cd628db1d2c34ebbb5835e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db3527e684a25b932d0774c8848b1ca</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896748</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Format Properties">
      <data key="d0">Format Properties</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Format Properties are a key element in Allplan software, encompassing various attributes such as pen thickness, line type, and line color that are assigned to layers and design elements. These properties play a vital role in defining the visual characteristics and overall appearance of content, particularly in architectural drawings. They not only influence the aesthetic qualities of design elements but also contribute to the organization and structuring of projects.

The concept of Format Properties extends to the features and settings that can be modified to adjust how elements are displayed within the software interface. These attributes are essential for formatting graphical elements, ensuring that visual styles are consistent and adhere to guidelines within the design system. Additionally, Format Properties are discussed in instructional materials, indicating their significance in understanding how to utilize Allplan effectively.

Within a project context, Format Properties are crucial for efficient management and integration of data, affecting both the presentation and layout of the materials. By defining specific settings and characteristics that dictate how content is arranged, they enhance the quality and functionality of graphical outputs. Overall, Format Properties are integral for both the formatting of text and the visual representation of design in Allplan, ensuring that projects are executed with clarity and precision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ef853aad5cd628db1d2c34ebbb5835e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c9198643b99c59d271fc71c45c3c2ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1a5cc1a53a54df5bb42dbbbe4bf2a83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3312cf4fab55427b11a562c6e43da9c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e51e7bae74af0b0a490800f2339aec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd8e342afc7b46634cae508eaa15f52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7098321c2776e7e778c6bbb3c1ca42a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08b1cb665906a399fabd227b2adc731c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-366a4dedb24bb07caabf849a20af9dd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cbed245f2e768aefab648e0d9e76305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf30d3aabc4a18fabe6106f90e773ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e3eb6fcd318d8d6a5063eca6302b02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d147b7f30c87dd3cdfc26438b50a359b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda504f43dd9840ca6b52acd37cec254&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d191d9315aa9177c51238149973cea38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c1bb94e215bb8cbbc9805b15edd42f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-928205bd70b27c1de0be77bfebc5e054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42fa2ac25e8d82137090e36aeea955a6</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896597</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pen Thickness">
      <data key="d0">Pen Thickness</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pen Thickness refers to a critical setting in the Allplan software that determines the thickness of lines drawn in technical drawings and designs. This setting can be customized for different elements, allowing users to choose from various thickness levels to achieve the desired presentation and clarity in their graphics.

As a format property, pen thickness is specifically related to the width of lines and is established in the Format section of the software's properties panel. Notably, the default setting for pen thickness is typically configured at 0.25. This particular attribute plays an essential role in the overall aesthetic and functional aspects of construction documents, influencing how these documents are perceived during presentations as well as in printed formats.

In summary, Pen Thickness is not only a configuration setting within Allplan but also an integral aspect of format properties that affects line widths in drawings, emphasizing its importance in graphic and drafting applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c5287c4c8d2cc121dff7af4c8f5b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9dd28f0f469bfa0a19a2e734ea5355a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daf5eae8ae425042459bcc9090c9b4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef05815e1db28bf2bfa21e6ebd99aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf30d3aabc4a18fabe6106f90e773ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e3eb6fcd318d8d6a5063eca6302b02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0041828ceff3158c0eb1286bf8b2c9d2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896603</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Color">
      <data key="d0">Color</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Color in Allplan represents visual characteristics assigned to various elements, which can be adjusted based on layers or pen settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Color is an icon displaying a color wheel, used in the user interface to manage formatting properties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c5287c4c8d2cc121dff7af4c8f5b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-48572244f863c525263d6644c196d230</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896848</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Line Type">
      <data key="d0">Line Type</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Line Type is a classification in Allplan that defines how lines are displayed, consisting of combinations of solid and spaced sections.&lt;SEP&gt;Line type is a format property that defines the style of lines in Allplan, such as solid, dashed, etc.&lt;SEP&gt;Line Type refers to the different styles of lines, such as continuous and dashed, used in technical drawings and architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Line type is a configurable option in the Format section of the software properties panel, with a setting of 1.&lt;SEP&gt;Line Type refers to different styles of lines available in Allplan, influencing visual representation in design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c5287c4c8d2cc121dff7af4c8f5b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef05815e1db28bf2bfa21e6ebd99aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e3eb6fcd318d8d6a5063eca6302b02c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0041828ceff3158c0eb1286bf8b2c9d2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896827</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dimension Text">
      <data key="d0">Dimension Text</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dimension Text in Allplan includes the annotations used to describe measurements in drawings, which can have specific formatting rules.&lt;SEP&gt;Dimension Text refers to technical specifications regarding settings in a software environment, likely related to architecture or engineering design.&lt;SEP&gt;Dimension text is textual notation in technical drawings that conveys specific measurements and details associated with dimension lines.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c5287c4c8d2cc121dff7af4c8f5b95c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-daf5eae8ae425042459bcc9090c9b4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6abd232f051ae36261abe24ae2c56cc4</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896601</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Text Dialog Box">
      <data key="d0">Text Dialog Box</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Text Dialog Box in Allplan is where users define settings for text display, including color and pen thickness options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c5287c4c8d2cc121dff7af4c8f5b95c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888400</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TrueType Fonts">
      <data key="d0">TrueType Fonts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">TrueType Fonts are a type of font that can be used in Allplan for dimension text and other annotations with specific formatting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-9c5287c4c8d2cc121dff7af4c8f5b95c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888400</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OLE Objects">
      <data key="d0">OLE Objects</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">OLE Objects refer to a technology utilized within Allplan that enables the linking and embedding of various data types and objects within documents. This feature enhances the functionality of Allplan by allowing users to integrate external content directly from different applications, thereby improving design capabilities and document management.

OLE Objects can be edited within their original applications, yet modifications do not affect the source documents, preserving the integrity of the original files while facilitating a rich data interaction experience within Allplan. Their ability to incorporate various file formats further underscores their versatility as a tool for document functionality.

OLE Objects are categorized as advanced components crucial for enhancing the interaction between documents and other objects, providing users with the capability to manage these interactive elements effectively. Users are required to have a foundational knowledge of these components to utilize their full potential successfully. Discussed extensively in updates and analyses surrounding Allplan, particularly in version 2020, OLE Objects enable better content importation and integration, showcasing their importance in contemporary software tools.

Overall, OLE Objects represent a significant advance in software capabilities, streamlining the incorporation of multimedia and other data elements into the design and documentation processes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-722696e14943f4546267ecafc68e9e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f6d6c0fc9029b0a0cac77b61d25be98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2705dc98383cde48e236bb2ab1b3a5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cecd1b49f606131d4d18cd0e76c61871&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2570331c618730dde3dd4a6dbd84f2fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e3c3d999f05b5a4160deca39584a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fcb2b72043f064aaa5a8bc609bc7cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576c3215ea56fe5cc9972a12ea2b15f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9eacc1be00bb6ff90fa2c50d34f1cbfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0172f9be3dc2d4df447199bae366551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-281cf84ade42e93865ebf5c751809d7b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b32889348a99f1de9f928e13308889cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a1f1ab7ff6e8fea42aef4c70a70c4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff23f27183206bfa757e52e6f4a54491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe74dde9699eac946401b657bd7a3f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb027f4dae8b784ba6284678c58eb53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34bb4d1bece4c6b740881581c584792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fcf2c3c5934400b78bf2c37ac9eda8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94949a11445d74650a452d0168521a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bd6705cfaefef03f8699f824fb4db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-329ae55c7564bde35eacf43331a5f1ea</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896837</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="XRefs">
      <data key="d0">XRefs</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">XRefs, or external references, are a crucial feature within Allplan software that facilitates the linking and management of data across various documents. They are essential for structuring projects by allowing users to reference external documents, such as drawing or NDW files, enabling the reuse of elements without the need for re-entry. This functionality supports design workflows and project management by improving document organization and minimizing redundancy.

As advanced software tools, XRefs are examined in usage scenarios, highlighting their importance in enhancing usability within Allplan. They serve as a foundation for managing references between different components or drawings, which is particularly relevant in architectural contexts. XRefs are also integrated into the Allplan documentation, providing guidelines on effective management and utilization to ensure users can leverage their full potential within design processes.

In the context of Allplan, XRefs encompass methods for linking both external and internal files. They are designed to offer dynamic updates to documents, which helps maintain clarity and enhances understanding in technical documentation. However, their implementation may present limitations or require specific instructions for optimal use, as their effectiveness can vary based on the type of reference utilized.

XRefs play a significant role in the editing processes of Allplan, where they manage and facilitate the referencing of linked elements within projects. Users engage with XRefs to streamline workflows, making them an important consideration in any architectural or design task that involves document management and project structuring. Their presence in Allplan serves not only to improve inter-document connections but also contributes to overall project efficiency in CAD and design environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-722696e14943f4546267ecafc68e9e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2705dc98383cde48e236bb2ab1b3a5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3dd2c04758b241fff557a2bfca3766b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a1f1ab7ff6e8fea42aef4c70a70c4ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff23f27183206bfa757e52e6f4a54491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbe74dde9699eac946401b657bd7a3f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3fb027f4dae8b784ba6284678c58eb53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d34bb4d1bece4c6b740881581c584792&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e471556ac4a9eb96314bbffe0317dff9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0225c6cd0e0197356caa64c1376f21a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-748f533da3d267d04f6722117f39ce75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87eb4ff8907ed1c09c6bc6c66884cc02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cd5d8b6ba80f2660de244d56f843a84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d13c1ec6448a96927c3c38201c3f38bc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db9f2b00a52fb78ca1259b781b49e955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5fea1e8d3e93e26f6de725f67a11c6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba56bb28bde779ccfd0b2be72d920734&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42383b7d601458b559969a4728d4c32d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7c5194ee3a94282c0395bb4ac0365f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fc6700a1e54f9edddf3c3c6c74ff899&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd26995fac1f3997ccbc19374d4ff94e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc7369e990190f470d2d25f179aa12b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fcf2c3c5934400b78bf2c37ac9eda8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a94949a11445d74650a452d0168521a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5bd6705cfaefef03f8699f824fb4db9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-329ae55c7564bde35eacf43331a5f1ea</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896707</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Element Properties">
      <data key="d0">Element Properties</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Element Properties refer to attributes such as pen thickness, line type, and line color that define how elements are displayed in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Element Properties refer to adjustable parameters within a software interface related to design or architectural applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Element Properties refers to important features or characteristics discussed in relation to design entities in the architectural context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-722696e14943f4546267ecafc68e9e2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d989eadbd97ed8073e75227b06ce9c70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a789f6f9ddfb3c5b68ed9d65b75d54e</data>
