    <node id="Output Mode">
      <data key="d0">Output Mode</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Output mode pertains to the configuration settings for printing, including options like Print to file.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-451be9692297c28020f54c8273fd6dca</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888400</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="File Type">
      <data key="d0">File Type</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">File type refers to the specified format in which print files are saved during the layout printing process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-451be9692297c28020f54c8273fd6dca</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888400</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Output Log">
      <data key="d0">Output Log</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Output log is a record generated after printing all layouts, detailing which layouts were printed successfully.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-451be9692297c28020f54c8273fd6dca</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888400</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Print File">
      <data key="d0">Print File</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A print file is a digital file created from formatted layouts intended for printing, often defined by specific output settings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-451be9692297c28020f54c8273fd6dca</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Print File Dialog Box">
      <data key="d0">Print File Dialog Box</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The print file dialog box is an interface element where users can review and modify file names for layouts before printing.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-451be9692297c28020f54c8273fd6dca</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hatching">
      <data key="d0">Hatching</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hatching refers to a design technique commonly used in architectural drawing and representation. It serves multiple purposes, primarily to indicate different materials, textures, and to enhance aesthetic features within the drawings. This technique allows architects and designers to visually communicate various elements and characteristics of their designs by applying patterns to specific areas.

In addition to indicating materials, hatching affects the representation of scale in architectural layouts. Different hatching settings can modify line spacing and the overall appearance of the drawn elements, making it a vital tool for accurate graphical representation in both 2D and 3D architectural designs. The effectiveness of hatching lies in its ability to convey rich visual information succinctly, thereby influencing the interpretation of the drawings by stakeholders.

Moreover, hatching is often referenced in the context of architectural software. It encompasses specific operational instructions that guide users in generating consistent graphical representations, ensuring that the intended visual styles are accurately applied. This versatility in applications highlights hatching as an essential concept in the field of architecture and design, merging technical precision with artistic expression.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4bf0d199f8a6c6b2db7e1ece08f8e75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a007e42b9b683c4bb5c145f80014d5b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef654b1e3ef63a37895f103aab89d589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43da9c48f26a42e9668f66534481e33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-061fb125d2fb8a19e5a7710ea6cde4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3476a00b543615b3e38120a7ab3e063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c8d72456e894846d3deadd295b27702&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ad8f9853fc194bce492007ac87533dc</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896773</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Adjust to Scale in Layout">
      <data key="d0">Adjust to Scale in Layout</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Adjust to Scale in Layout is a hatching setting that allows for dynamic changes in line spacing with scale adjustments in layout designs.&lt;SEP&gt;The "Adjust to Scale in Layout" setting determines how patterns in architectural designs adapt based on reference scales.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjust to Scale in Layout refers to the setting that modifies hatching appearance based on scale settings.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjust to Scale in Layout describes the principle of modifying hatching line density based on the dimensional scale depicted.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjust to Scale in Layout is a hatching setting that influences line spacing relative to different scales in architectural design.&lt;SEP&gt;Adjust to scale in layout is a method that modifies the display of patterns according to their scale.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4bf0d199f8a6c6b2db7e1ece08f8e75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf93c97b7398da09d1cabc644a3e194&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7ce74ea6ecc7ed8833abf30be6ca9da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eea8f43d85f3143da139b66b4027e324&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ba44b194cfdbf9ae71ac6e1e2b997c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-872f02b2795740e33f336688f7d1bdf2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896775</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Constant in Layout">
      <data key="d0">Constant in Layout</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Constant in Layout is a hatching setting where the spacing between hatching lines remains constant despite changes in scale.&lt;SEP&gt;The 'Constant in layout; as set in defaults' option ensures that line spacing remains unchanged irrespective of scale adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Constant in Layout refers to a setting that maintains hatching appearance regardless of scale adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Constant in Layout refers to the principle of maintaining consistent hatching line styles despite dimension changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Constant in Layout is a hatching setting that impacts the representation of hatching in layouts and documents.&lt;SEP&gt;Constant in layout is a setting that determines how patterns are displayed without adjustment to scale.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4bf0d199f8a6c6b2db7e1ece08f8e75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db13cd4f3d63a7d5220eeab390c23fbd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7ce74ea6ecc7ed8833abf30be6ca9da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eea8f43d85f3143da139b66b4027e324&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ba44b194cfdbf9ae71ac6e1e2b997c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-872f02b2795740e33f336688f7d1bdf2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896772</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Reference Scale">
      <data key="d0">Reference Scale</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Reference Scale is a value used in layouts to adjust line spacing and patterns accurately according to the desired scaling factor.&lt;SEP&gt;Reference scale is an adjustable parameter for line spacing, shown as '100.00' in the interface.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4bf0d199f8a6c6b2db7e1ece08f8e75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5be17e6e205509889b8ba2a61070a3</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896778</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hatching Defaults">
      <data key="d0">Hatching Defaults</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Hatching Defaults are preset parameters that define the behavior of hatching applied to components regarding spacing and appearance.&lt;SEP&gt;Hatching defaults are settings that help ensure users can adapt their drawings effectively according to scale requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4bf0d199f8a6c6b2db7e1ece08f8e75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f24028c3171a221367540a5865d66d32</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896776</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pattern">
      <data key="d0">Pattern</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pattern relates to the design elements used in layouts that can vary in size and number based on scaling settings and defaults.&lt;SEP&gt;Pattern refers to the repeated decorative design used in architectural design software.&lt;SEP&gt;A pattern is an arrangement of shapes or elements; in this context, it consists of interlocking diamond or lattice-shaped elements demonstrated in two different scales.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4bf0d199f8a6c6b2db7e1ece08f8e75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-061fb125d2fb8a19e5a7710ea6cde4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3509d31878123c232371f68a6bab9059</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896770</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pattern Defaults">
      <data key="d0">Pattern Defaults</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Pattern Defaults define the initial size and specifications for patterns used in layout design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4bf0d199f8a6c6b2db7e1ece08f8e75</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pattern Parameters">
      <data key="d0">Pattern Parameters</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Pattern Parameters allow for specific adjustments to the height and width of pattern elements within layouts.&lt;SEP&gt;Pattern parameters determine the specifications for layout element dimensions and placement in a design context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a4bf0d199f8a6c6b2db7e1ece08f8e75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bf93c97b7398da09d1cabc644a3e194</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Filter Step by Step Dialog Box">
      <data key="d0">Filter Step by Step Dialog Box</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Filter Step by Step Dialog Box allows users to apply filters to the objects or elements they wish to select.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abb11ec0fcfe86b8f7442326222d5684</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Document Area">
      <data key="d0">Document Area</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Document Area displays the name and path of the drawing file or custom NDW file associated with selected elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abb11ec0fcfe86b8f7442326222d5684</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Elements List Box">
      <data key="d0">Elements List Box</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Elements List Box displays the objects or elements available for selection and modification in Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abb11ec0fcfe86b8f7442326222d5684</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Match Property Button">
      <data key="d0">Match Property Button</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Match Property Button is a tool that allows users to match specific properties of elements within the Properties Palette.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abb11ec0fcfe86b8f7442326222d5684</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Match Group Button">
      <data key="d0">Match Group Button</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Match Group Button matches all properties of a selected group of elements, facilitating bulk property management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abb11ec0fcfe86b8f7442326222d5684</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Match All Button">
      <data key="d0">Match All Button</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Match All Button matches all properties except geometric properties of selected elements, streamlining the editing process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-abb11ec0fcfe86b8f7442326222d5684</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
