    </node>
    <node id="Drag-and-Drop Editing">
      <data key="d0">Drag-and-Drop Editing</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Drag-and-drop editing is a feature that allows documents to be moved or copied through a simple click and drag action.&lt;SEP&gt;Drag-and-drop editing is a feature within ProjectPilot that allows users to easily manipulate data through intuitive actions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d084f8d91bd7ea701e82581899432ab3</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896860</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Preview">
      <data key="d0">Preview</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Preview feature allows users to see a document's contents in different views and offers specific options for zooming and panning.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Import Dialog Box">
      <data key="d0">Import Dialog Box</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Import dialog box is a function that allows users to specify file types and folders from which they want to import data.&lt;SEP&gt;The Import Dialog Box in Allplan allows users to select files for import, presenting a hierarchical view of storage locations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Import Dialog Box is specifically designed for file importation settings and options within software applications like Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a71675f17feba1decb70c72f6bba6979&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fd23629614922098d992bcd4a623393</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896861</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="File Types">
      <data key="d0">File Types</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">File types refer to the various formats that can be used for importing and exporting data, such as .dwg, .dxf, .svg, etc.&lt;SEP&gt;File Types refers to various categories for importing and exporting files within the presented context.&lt;SEP&gt;File Types denote the various formats that data and documents can have, impacting their utilization in software like Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;File types pertain to the formats of files that can be imported or exported, which are discussed in relation to data handling.&lt;SEP&gt;File Types are categories that define formats used for storing data in computing, which may relate to the context of the discarded content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a007e42b9b683c4bb5c145f80014d5b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59b7bf09cf4a352e9493ab3525a3ace7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b68f2ca938a6dbe6997cf15aa9e63e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e2c26be1a94c8eed1818a256f2051b7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896710</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Large Coordinates">
      <data key="d0">Large Coordinates</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Large coordinates refer to data points with high numerical values, which can cause issues during data processing in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Large coordinates refer to data points that require specific handling during data operations, highlighted in the analysis of discarded content.&lt;SEP&gt;Large coordinates are numerical values that require specific management techniques during file conversions to ensure accurate point measurements.&lt;SEP&gt;Large Coordinates refer to the unique challenges and considerations involved in managing extensive coordinate systems in design software like Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76b68f2ca938a6dbe6997cf15aa9e63e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3aadfc905cd8139b833a90823c6bf21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a75742c184cc0dbc6628913a961abf</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896862</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DWG Files">
      <data key="d0">DWG Files</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">DWG files are a type of file used in CAD (Computer-Aided Design) applications to represent two-dimensional and three-dimensional designs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DXF Files">
      <data key="d0">DXF Files</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">DXF files are drawing exchange format files that enable data interoperability between CAD applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="DGN Files">
      <data key="d0">DGN Files</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">DGN files are design files used by MicroStation and other CAD applications, primarily for engineering and architectural drawings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888402</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="HPGL2 Files">
      <data key="d0">HPGL2 Files</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">HPGL2 files are plotter files used for printing CAD designs effectively.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888402</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="SVG Files">
      <data key="d0">SVG Files</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">SVG files are Scalable Vector Graphics files used for two-dimensional vector graphics.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888402</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="ODX Interfaces">
      <data key="d0">ODX Interfaces</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">ODX interfaces are tools that facilitate the conversion of files between various formats for use in Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4bb7084078428520dac0dda21740c62c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888402</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layer">
      <data key="d0">Layer</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Layer is a conceptual model in Allplan 2020 that manages elements and data organization within a project, allowing for better visualization and control over the design.&lt;SEP&gt;Layers are organizational structures in Allplan that help manage the format properties of elements used in drawings.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer is a functional aspect within the document structure used to organize different elements within the layout.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer represents a column in the table detailing the different layers that objects can be assigned to.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer refers to a fundamental component within graphic software that allows for the organization and manipulation of graphical elements independently.&lt;SEP&gt;The Layer setting, labeled as DE_GEN01 (General01), is included in the Format section of the software properties panel.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer is an organizational concept in design software where elements can inherit properties from the layer's line style.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a007e42b9b683c4bb5c145f80014d5b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef853aad5cd628db1d2c34ebbb5835e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1a5cc1a53a54df5bb42dbbbe4bf2a83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39a02f8aff31c62fad850e279e70ded8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5eb8054aa416fc36085a64f4f7a82fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef05815e1db28bf2bfa21e6ebd99aaf</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896615</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Selection Rectangle">
      <data key="d0">Selection Rectangle</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">Selection Rectangle is a tool or method used to enclose elements for zooming in on specific parts of the design within a viewport.&lt;SEP&gt;A selection rectangle is a visual tool used to select multiple elements within a defined area in Allplan drawings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Selection Rectangle is a graphical interface tool used to select multiple elements by drawing a rectangle on the screen.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d202d87f74ec6d653a0d9a932427c930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2e09e8bba60f1d58ef71be4e357ed2a</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888402</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Line Color">
      <data key="d0">Line Color</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Line color is a format property that specifies the color used for lines and shapes in Allplan drawings.&lt;SEP&gt;Line color is a design property option in the Format section, marked as 1 and indicated by a black color box.&lt;SEP&gt;Line Color is a format property in Allplan that defines the color of lines in a drawing.&lt;SEP&gt;Line Color is a design attribute that can affect visual output and text formatting in Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9dd28f0f469bfa0a19a2e734ea5355a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ef05815e1db28bf2bfa21e6ebd99aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e3eb6fcd318d8d6a5063eca6302b02c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896593</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Dimension Lines">
      <data key="d0">Dimension Lines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Dimension lines are lines used in drawings to indicate measurements and sizes of elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Dimension lines are graphical representations in technical drawings that indicate measurements related to objects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6abd232f051ae36261abe24ae2c56cc4</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896603</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Filter Assistant Toolbar">
      <data key="d0">Filter Assistant Toolbar</data>
      <data key="d1">tool</data>
      <data key="d2">The Filter Assistant Toolbar is a toolbar that provides tools for filtering and selecting elements in the software interface.&lt;SEP&gt;The Filter Assistant Toolbar provides tools to help users select and manage elements more effectively in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Filter Assistant Toolbar is a specific tool mentioned that aids users in the selection process within the Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;The Filter Assistant Toolbar is part of the user interface that includes selection tools to help users specify selection regions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Filter Assistant Toolbar is a user interface option that aids in the selection process within a software application by offering various filtering options.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2dc8dbb1ae85aa5a5ee5c845f4b8bbfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d202d87f74ec6d653a0d9a932427c930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c63378d2861e5872e217e66366c405b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246815af5194a5328daf62dbd8cb24be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae8832a2783b4ebb13fc2190697157d7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896640</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Basic CAD Knowledge">
      <data key="d0">Basic CAD Knowledge</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Basic CAD knowledge is a foundational understanding necessary for users to effectively operate Allplan 2020 for architectural and engineering tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888402</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Documentation">
      <data key="d0">Documentation</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentation refers to a comprehensive array of written materials that provide essential information and guidance for users of software, particularly the Allplan software suite. This documentation serves as a critical resource, offering installation instructions, detailed descriptions of tools, and guidance on user interface elements. Within the framework of Allplan, it addresses various aspects such as system requirements, user feedback, and help with installation, aiming to enhance user understanding and experience.

The documentation encompasses not only the functionalities and features of Allplan software but also emphasizes instructional materials that guide users in data management practices and operational tactics. It provides significant insights into specific tools, including viewport tools and the Actionbar, ensuring users are well-equipped to navigate the software effectively.

Additionally, the documentation discusses procedures for managing backups, navigating printing workflows, and handling files in various formats, which is crucial for effective software usage. It seeks to facilitate clarity and comprehensiveness, allowing users to fully grasp the software's capabilities and streamline their experience with the various functionalities offered by Allplan. 

In summary, Documentation is an indispensable guide that aids users in understanding and utilizing Allplan software to its fullest potential, enhancing both user experience and operational efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e575527346b06bf6c21d3b7006a63ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7350b2b780ae75fe6e836c03d017ae91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cac8b97ea5b887e17ce4d3b20d414b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60f2f16a99d8ed5edf18e8f8fefa073c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8770676b478170be4fb1a0b71a7b991e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d5646ef98bb7be82dcf45cb8ed8ea46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ead411bc27ddadc770622c6d9da2f37c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ac92338ff12f2149503471780d9b2af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee2fbf036ff7cc08e147865140c827af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40ccd0d67812471dbe1e7e27ccf9a892&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34bf5f454cde4e8bc980db586539c9ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f22c7d4278cd63fdbd7cf9330981f92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0a5a563641004c6d994354e64bbdd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc81bbce7f6732d5f7cf3b0c3a9f19e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e60e08936a9c34cbeef4c292ce8e7f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65e4a09f41d26cbe4cd420156b9434b7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896677</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Architecture Tutorial">
      <data key="d0">Architecture Tutorial</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Architecture Tutorial is a guided resource within Allplan 2020 that assists users in designing buildings and analyzing building data.&lt;SEP&gt;The Architecture Tutorial provides step-by-step guidance for designing buildings and analyzing building data.&lt;SEP&gt;Architecture Tutorial is the main heading of the interface showing structural levels of a building model in the Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;Architecture Tutorial is a node in the file tree that represents instructional content related to architectural design.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aef18e4906ae04faffda048cb70ce961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3562d6726fa0bbac3b7eebc748987816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4633e4c71d2db6ddf873662d52285a65</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896739</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Engineering Tutorial">
      <data key="d0">Engineering Tutorial</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Engineering Tutorial provides step-by-step instructions on creating key plans and drawings within Allplan 2020 for engineering purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;The Engineering Tutorial offers step-by-step instructions for creating key plans, general arrangement drawings, and reinforcement drawings.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aef18e4906ae04faffda048cb70ce961</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888402</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Help Feature">
      <data key="d0">Help Feature</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">The Help Feature within Allplan 2020 allows users to access assistance for current tools through F1 or an interactive help interface.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-16d3d7723ac4866caa16109031e971f2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888402</data>
      <data key="d6" />
