    <node id="Task List">
      <data key="d0">Task List</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The task list indicates the priority rating of each task and contains details that can be defined in the Details palette.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec22abab62a86e389dc5d86bb0bf9c04</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888403</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Details Palette">
      <data key="d0">Details Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Details palette allows users to find and edit all details of a task and view the priority rating.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec22abab62a86e389dc5d86bb0bf9c04</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888403</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layers Palette">
      <data key="d0">Layers Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">The Layers Palette enables users to monitor and alter the status of design layers in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Layers Palette displays the layer hierarchy and allows users to define visibility and status of layers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Layers Palette is a tool mentioned in the context of software that requires understanding installation procedures for effective use.&lt;SEP&gt;The Layers palette is an element of Allplan's user interface, aiding in the management of different layers within the software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec22abab62a86e389dc5d86bb0bf9c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1729b2d3689ebe861c41881a390fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5c46f34c6b261b8f317bfaa2af9de2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f694199f09ad57655300ad9493ce164</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896866</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layer Visibility">
      <data key="d0">Layer Visibility</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Layer visibility refers to the settings that define whether layers are visible, hidden, or modifiable.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer visibility is a functionality in Allplan that allows users to manipulate the visibility of different project layers.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer visibility refers to the management aspects of layers within Allplan software, crucial for effective design workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer visibility is a task associated with managing layers in the Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;Layer visibility refers to the ability to show or hide layers within design software, an important feature for streamlining user workflows.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec22abab62a86e389dc5d86bb0bf9c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b38a359a9fc91218dfcdcfb75fa56e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4135e5fd8b98b66b5a6b0da1dfdb4cae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3cc1f914a850b6c5593ff6fa507c8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a76283f28a4b943e6457ebc556192fa8</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896735</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Favorite Files">
      <data key="d0">Favorite Files</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Favorite files allow users to save and retrieve specific layer settings for convenient access.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec22abab62a86e389dc5d86bb0bf9c04</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888403</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Modules Palette">
      <data key="d0">Modules Palette</data>
      <data key="d1">component</data>
      <data key="d2">The Modules Palette allows for quick switching between various task areas within Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Modules Palette is used to switch between different task areas within the software configuration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Modules Palette is a part of Allplan's user interface, likely containing various functional elements for users to interact with.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-ec22abab62a86e389dc5d86bb0bf9c04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1729b2d3689ebe861c41881a390fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d19f218012d660f7aab6742d06b028fe</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896889</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Coordinates">
      <data key="d0">Coordinates</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Coordinates are numerical values representing specific locations in site plans, which are legally binding in project documentation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888403</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Settings Dialog Box">
      <data key="d0">Settings Dialog Box</data>
      <data key="d1">interface</data>
      <data key="d2">The Settings Dialog Box in Allplan is used to define parameters for coordinating and adjusting units and length during data conversion.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888403</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Unit Parameter">
      <data key="d0">Unit Parameter</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Unit Parameter indicates the measurement unit (e.g., mm, cm) for coordinate and length values during data conversion in Allplan.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888403</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Layout Scale">
      <data key="d0">Layout Scale</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Layout Scale is a setting that controls visual elements such as text size and spacing when converting files between systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Layout Scale refers to the scale factor used for layout design within the software, indicated as 1x with a value of 100 in the dialog.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd8e75fbc99abf7ad1b346372b05508</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896595</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Resizing Factor">
      <data key="d0">Resizing Factor</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Resizing Factor is a parameter that allows for adjusting the size of coordinates and lengths during data conversion to match different units.&lt;SEP&gt;Resizing Factor is a control setting in the software that adjusts the enlargement or reduction of coordinates and length values, set to 1.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bd8e75fbc99abf7ad1b346372b05508</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896596</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Configuration Files">
      <data key="d0">Configuration Files</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Configuration Files store the mappings and settings necessary for converting data between different software systems using Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration files are files used to set parameters and configurations for various software systems, relevant in design processes.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration files are essential components of software operations, referenced in the context of data exchange and management procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration Files pertain to settings that can influence the exporting and importing of data in CAD environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Configuration files are text files used in software applications to define settings, parameters, and behaviors during installation and operation.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-570d3bc3171e99dff9f87a65b112a960&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d2bcf1c612666251acc2f53393922b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a16694a13961fdd8f050ecabaca7848a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4c8791dcb306d3419c6dc1f6d3bb00c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896626</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Exchange Favorites">
      <data key="d0">Exchange Favorites</data>
      <data key="d1">other</data>
      <data key="d2">Exchange Favorites are predefined options in Allplan that provide optimal settings for import and export of data to simplify workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;Exchange Favorites is a section within the settings dialog where users can select and manage export options for drawing files.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31a3196d9c94c23fbe21c202d6923681</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896620</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Prototype File">
      <data key="d0">Prototype File</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">A Prototype File in Allplan contains essential default resources and layer names that facilitate correct data exports to AutoCAD.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888404</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="AutoCAD">
      <data key="d0">AutoCAD</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">AutoCAD is a software application renowned for its capabilities in computer-aided design (CAD) and drafting, widely utilized across multiple fields such as architecture and engineering. It enables users to create precise drawings and models, contributing significantly to efficient design workflows and project execution.

In the realm of architecture, AutoCAD is particularly valued for its drawing and layout management functionalities, which allow architects to develop detailed and organized design documents. The software not only aids in the creation of these documents but also supports the management of layout data vital for successful project outcomes.

Moreover, AutoCAD is noted for its emphasis on interoperability, requiring users to understand various file formats to ensure proper data exchange with other software applications. This aspect of AutoCAD is critical, especially when collaborating with other design tools or adhering to industry standards such as the Industry Foundation Classes (IFC), highlighting the software's role in facilitating seamless data transfer methodologies.

Overall, AutoCAD stands as a pivotal tool in the design and drafting industries, marrying advanced technical capabilities with a focus on effective data interchange and collaborative functionality.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-817a49bc4b129f4601e73d18a2402996&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20ca43a5078c0cb201783352641cc976&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0961b3887e3e64a8b3be23985cd3300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-570d3bc3171e99dff9f87a65b112a960&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6b83aa637cd34755e8ef37374cf3ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4613aef76feff60ae50ccfc83b43f347&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1710ee37e8dbe9125820f0b81b80de4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d2c04071e9f1f4696012b1d8f769748</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896620</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="External Path Folder">
      <data key="d0">External Path Folder</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The External Path Folder is a location for accessing more files with library elements in a software environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The External Path Folder signifies paths outside of the current setup in Allplan 2020, represented by an orange network path icon.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026f24b87030d011599249910d81669f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896851</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Predefined Settings">
      <data key="d0">Predefined Settings</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Predefined Settings provide default sorting criteria to organize objects in the Objects Palette.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888404</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Sorting Criteria">
      <data key="d0">Sorting Criteria</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Sorting Criteria are specific parameters used to categorize and arrange objects in the Objects Palette based on user preferences or predefined options.&lt;SEP&gt;Sorting Criteria pertains to the parameters or standards used to arrange data or objects in a specific order, such as layers or attributes in drawing files.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db9d1d630b7b7e79232c951497ff754c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896759</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Control Buttons">
      <data key="d0">Control Buttons</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Control Buttons are options within the Objects Palette that enable users to manage the visibility, selection, and display settings of objects.&lt;SEP&gt;Control Buttons are elements within the software interface that allow user interactions and functionalities related to the content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1649ba5aab72b8db5597324f704210e4</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896765</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Transparency Setting">
      <data key="d0">Transparency Setting</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Transparency Setting determines the visibility of objects in terms of their opacity levels, affecting their appearance in the animation view type.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888404</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Animation View Type">
      <data key="d0">Animation View Type</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Animation View Type defines the visual presentation of objects during animations, influenced by settings like transparency.&lt;SEP&gt;Animation View Type indicates the display mode affecting how users visualize animated objects within the software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1d59584cb0afc041ab57b7f98deb5234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-238b154db59fc88f53f1e705f54a803f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896771</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Brackets">
      <data key="d0">Brackets</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Brackets refer to a tool used in selection to group elements for simultaneous selection in a graphical interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Brackets are among the selection methods used to facilitate the selection of elements in a user interface.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d202d87f74ec6d653a0d9a932427c930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bea4ecbf369f8e5a0a1e8e93a7608c9</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896653</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mouse">
      <data key="d0">Mouse</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Mouse is an input device used for navigating and interacting with the user interface, especially in viewport navigation modes.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse is a pointing device used to interact with elements in a software interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse is the input device referenced for interacting with the software’s tools for drawing polylines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mouse is an input device referenced in the content for its operational capabilities and required installation procedures.&lt;SEP&gt;Mouse is identified as a drafting tool whose interactions are outlined in a table detailing its functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mouse is a device used for navigating and selecting elements in a digital interface.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d202d87f74ec6d653a0d9a932427c930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2e09e8bba60f1d58ef71be4e357ed2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a26c096ae289b75e162c75435a2ad81c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-066285e75861d3826b454c75c37304d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12895911e0d951eda4f327a1d0d3636b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5336772abb1e6a10869aa4432fd948</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896736</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Element Info">
      <data key="d0">Element Info</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Element Info refers to the additional information displayed about selected elements, including names and layers, within the graphical interface.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d202d87f74ec6d653a0d9a932427c930</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888404</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Filters">
      <data key="d0">Filters</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Filters are tools used to limit the selection of elements based on specific properties or types in order to streamline the selection process.&lt;SEP&gt;Filters are tools within the user interface that allow users to display or manipulate certain elements based on specific criteria.&lt;SEP&gt;Filters are tools used in design software that help users refine selection processes and manage elements in a design layout.&lt;SEP&gt;Filters are tools that help users refine the selection of drawing elements based on specific properties, enhancing the selection process in a software environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Filters refer to categories or options that could relate to the organization of content, mentioned in the context of the analysis but not elaborated upon.&lt;SEP&gt;Filters refer to functions or features in software that allow users to isolate or manage specific data or visual elements based on criteria.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d202d87f74ec6d653a0d9a932427c930&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64220d8c6a507cb0154d5cab89b3a5f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5108d2e2b72daaad428ddab42780961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83025285bd3f673f9649869b8d01d3df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66aae6d0a1f05602b15cedde6bda0685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f62793877b09c086c32620ffe91719d5</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896671</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="SmartPart">
      <data key="d0">SmartPart</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">SmartPart refers to a feature or tool used within a software environment, representing a type of component or object that enhances functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;SmartPart refers to modular design components within Allplan that include architectural elements like doors and windows, which can be customized.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c36ab84e987861cbb78ee2d63372f5cd</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896840</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Terrain Point">
      <data key="d0">Terrain Point</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Terrain Point represents a specific type of point in a terrain modeling context, defined by a shortcut menu for easy entry.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888404</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="XRef">
      <data key="d0">XRef</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">XRef is a comparative feature used in software for managing references, including normal and advanced XRefs for data linking and editing.&lt;SEP&gt;XRef refers to a functionality or guideline related to referencing in a broader context, typically associated with Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;XRef is a file type in the Allplan environment that facilitates the organization of projects and documents.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8199187eb67f52e7222ebf37021902&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0225c6cd0e0197356caa64c1376f21a4</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896708</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Allplan Application">
      <data key="d0">Allplan Application</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Allplan Application is the software application that includes features like viewport management, tool palettes, and user interface configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Allplan Application is a software that includes features and functionalities connected to the Actionbar and its components.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e67a50ed6b2a13c3444d6060a41c4478</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896832</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Direct Object Modification (DOM)">
      <data key="d0">Direct Object Modification (DOM)</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Direct Object Modification (DOM) is a technique that enables direct alterations to objects within a software environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888404</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="CursorTips">
      <data key="d0">CursorTips</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">CursorTips is a feature within the Allplan software that serves as a visual aid to enhance user interaction with point detection types and snapping functionalities. It provides intelligent cursor assistance, allowing for increased precision during user interactions, particularly when drawing or placing points in the software’s graphical interface.

These interface elements include visual or textual cues that support users as they work, ensuring they can accurately utilize point snapping features. By appearing within the snap radius, CursorTips facilitate a seamless drawing experience, empowering users to make precise placements and adjustments within their design projects. 

Overall, CursorTips is integral to improving interaction and functionality in Allplan, particularly in the realm of construction design and drafting, making it a valuable tool for users looking to enhance their drawing accuracy and efficiency.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-17c659d529ac707dbae01a6773c0c4d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38d959099d4c65fdc7bb2119334ec31e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f82e0207f6c5657ed5590659ca3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b0f09d2ce2c133ac20dc536700c0f11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e637fc0a6aaa19a2e54eef0d67d0638&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6375b111b5a548a3ecea298900699ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36a28cc7cd4b71b973ca7e039ff7448a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f3618377e998809ae5639b5b22136d</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896792</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Smart Symbol File">
      <data key="d0">Smart Symbol File</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A Smart Symbol File is a file format (.nmk) used to save smart symbols within the Allplan library or any other folder.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d305d677976b85ecf574260a9460d5b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763888404</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Resizing Points">
      <data key="d0">Resizing Points</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Resizing Points are specific points defined in smart symbols that allow for dynamic resizing of the design elements during modifications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2d305d677976b85ecf574260a9460d5b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
