    <node id="Viewports">
      <data key="d0">Viewports</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Viewports are sections of the user interface where users can see and edit design models, with options for different views and configurations.&lt;SEP&gt;Viewports are another user interface component relevant to Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;Viewports are sections of the user interface that display different perspectives or portions of a model.&lt;SEP&gt;Viewports are a design element discussed in relation to model manipulation within design software, though the details of their function and application are not provided in the discarded content.&lt;SEP&gt;Viewports refers to a term used in design and drawing, but lacks substantive detail and context in the discarded content.&lt;SEP&gt;Viewports refers to functionalities within software that manage visual representations, critical for graphical design or architectural modeling.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-b2e09e8bba60f1d58ef71be4e357ed2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2811ca6e09d4513b3fef90682a011dbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f08b9a1671199a929dedf70ef971350f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59363ccfd543ba9b7444cdd35e345fdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24be5c2e8e4697c2c0c6124d3c2a4a24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb87002bbceda800e1cfa558349e5230</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
