    <node id="IFC Data">
      <data key="d0">IFC Data</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">IFC Data refers to the information structure used in building models, compatible with various software tools for planning.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC data refers to Industry Foundation Classes data used in Building Information Modeling to facilitate interoperability between software applications.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC Data refers to Industry Foundation Classes data, which are used for data management in architectural modeling workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC data refers to data related to the Industry Foundation Classes, which facilitates interoperability in building and construction workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC Data refers to data formatted according to the Industry Foundation Classes standard, commonly used in building information modeling (BIM) processes.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC Data pertains to a framework for exchanging information in construction and architecture, though the specific content lacks detail in the text.</data>
