    <node id="Linear Snap">
      <data key="d0">Linear Snap</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Linear Snap is a feature in Allplan that allows for placing points in alignment with existing points using specific mouse actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear Snap is a technique used in drafting that helps with aligning design entities using snapping points.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear Snap refers to a feature in design software that aids in aligning elements but is not elaborated in the discarded content.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear Snap is a tool feature discussed in the context of drawing programs, aiding in precision drawing and alignment.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear snap is a key principle used for aligning points in drafting, essential for achieving precision in artwork and technical drawing.&lt;SEP&gt;Linear Snap is mentioned as part of surrounding content, likely relating to techniques or functionalities in a design context.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38d959099d4c65fdc7bb2119334ec31e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01313bfcae15245d50297b37059f3b16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-249e6b447c5cc69c30d1fdb9bcaf7ce4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3af48dcb63ba4c0626612d35b84747e5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96933dce8a9277b35ee767ec3cbd877d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb512be684eed9d9d59ae9c605e6b55f</data>
