    <node id="Snap Radius">
      <data key="d0">Snap Radius</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Snap Radius defines the distance within which Allplan detects points for snapping when drawing.&lt;SEP&gt;The snap radius is a defined area around the intersection point that indicates the effective range for snapping functions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Snap Radius indicates a circular zone around the crosshairs, where snapping operations occur.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38d959099d4c65fdc7bb2119334ec31e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e345697d6ea758737ad13d83a73b299a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01313bfcae15245d50297b37059f3b16</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896790</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Grid">
      <data key="d0">Grid</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Grid is a tool in Allplan used to provide visual orientation and assist with point snapping during design tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Grid refers to a structure in drawing applications that assists in layout and precision, facilitating the alignment of elements within the drawing space.&lt;SEP&gt;The Grid is a structural element mentioned in relation to improving alignment and precision in drawing projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38d959099d4c65fdc7bb2119334ec31e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96933dce8a9277b35ee767ec3cbd877d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bb512be684eed9d9d59ae9c605e6b55f</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
