      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Point Snapping">
      <data key="d0">Point Snapping</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Point Snapping is a technique utilized in various design and drafting software, including Allplan, to facilitate the accurate positioning and alignment of points in relation to existing elements within a workspace. This functionality enhances precision during drawing operations by allowing users to snap to defined points or measurements, ensuring that elements are aligned correctly.

In graphical design, Point Snapping provides a method that helps users achieve a higher level of accuracy when placing points and aligning objects within a user interface. By interacting with specified points on a grid, Point Snapping optimizes the drawing process, providing visual feedback that assists in the placement of points and elements.

Moreover, Point Snapping is integral to computer-aided design (CAD) software, where it aids in aligning elements with specified coordinates or fixed points. This method not only improves workflow efficiency but also helps prevent errors during the design process, making it a critical component in the tools used by designers and engineers.

Overall, Point Snapping is a vital feature in design software that supports users in creating precise and professional-grade drawings by ensuring accurate alignment and placement of points throughout the drafting process.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38d959099d4c65fdc7bb2119334ec31e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-625701e5ecf336500c6ce794dba12de8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36a28cc7cd4b71b973ca7e039ff7448a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01313bfcae15245d50297b37059f3b16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c8ba27c8b9aa5a0a41c53b0f10aa51b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60e659310c035f39edf5895e7ed6022e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a5fb3518984234d6291e952cf809e13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd8d5da24155e24553032d0f1760a316&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2e01cbfdc9ad4fe9bbe7de0777b3246&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-769e9951ddc7536ab2c03c5dbe94dbcb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c145032969306b2dc3113e1f39fcea29</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896791</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Crosshairs">
      <data key="d0">Crosshairs</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Crosshairs refer to the graphical indicators that help users align points more effectively in Allplan during drawing operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Crosshairs are visual markers used to indicate the focal point for snapping and are oriented both horizontally and vertically through the center of the snap radius.&lt;SEP&gt;The crosshairs marked as (A) serve as the central reference points for snapping in the diagram.&lt;SEP&gt;Crosshairs are graphical indicators used in the software interface to assist users in aligning and placing points accurately in a workspace.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38d959099d4c65fdc7bb2119334ec31e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e345697d6ea758737ad13d83a73b299a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01313bfcae15245d50297b37059f3b16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c926d8f34f6208bc9f906828d61e12a</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896790</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
