    <node id="Installation Basics">
      <data key="d0">Installation Basics</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Installation Basics refers to a discarded section within technical documentation that encompasses foundational topics associated with the installation processes of software applications, particularly for tools like Allplan. This section likely serves as a header that introduces essential concepts or requirements for setting up software or systems, outlining the basic principles of installation procedures relevant to various users.

The content associated with Installation Basics appears to cover a variety of instructional aspects, including an introduction to the installation process of both software and hardware setups. It specifically mentions elements such as smart symbols and SmartParts within Allplan, indicating that it is tailored to users transitioning to more advanced functionalities within the software. Despite its relevance, the content has been marked as discarded, suggesting it may lack the detailed structure or organization required to be fully informative.

Furthermore, Installation Basics is noted for potentially discussing fundamental concepts in drawing software and architectural modeling, aiming to provide users with an understanding necessary for grasping further advanced topics. Although the content is noted for its simplistic structure, it nevertheless addresses core installation mechanics and the basic operational usage of the relevant software tools or applications.

In summary, Installation Basics encapsulates essential yet basic information concerning installation methodologies within the context of software applications, with a focus on Allplan, and its contents serve an instructional role, although ultimately rendered discarded due to probable limitations in detail and organization.</data>
