    <node id="Checkboxes">
      <data key="d0">Checkboxes</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Checkboxes are interactive elements in the user interface that allow users to select corresponding options for layer statuses.&lt;SEP&gt;Checkboxes are interactive elements within user interfaces that represent selection states and options for users.&lt;SEP&gt;Checkboxes are interactive elements in the software interface that allow users to select options for matching properties.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-a1a5cc1a53a54df5bb42dbbbe4bf2a83&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd71268589f15edbb236dfeee6bf99e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ea6874f69449311da64044dd62af723</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896614</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Content">
      <data key="d0">Content</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The term **Content** refers to various types of information and material analyzed within the context of documentation, particularly related to Allplan software. It encompasses a wide range of textual and visual elements, including instructional fragments, user guidance, and placeholders, many of which have been identified as discarded due to lacking sufficient context or relevance.

Content includes information presented in sections like "Installation" and "Basics," as well as other instructional material aimed at enhancing user understanding of the Allplan interface and functionalities. Examples include guidance on navigating user interface components, utilizing the Shortcut Menu, handling features like SmartParts, and instructions for polygonization within architectural design settings. 

A significant portion of the content analyzed consists of fragments marked as discarded which may feature as empty entries, numeric placeholders, or incoherent text that fail to convey meaningful information. For instance, entries containing numerical values, such as "23", "292", and other characters, appear to serve no functional purpose within the broader documentation context.

In addition to irrelevant fragments, the content also covers aspects of user feedback, action bars, and tutorials, providing insights into the functional organization of the software. The discarded elements may reflect attempts at discussing instructional elements or practices in data management, all of which contribute to understanding technical nuances in the software, despite their ultimate classification as non-informative.

Overall, Content represents both a critical examination of information and a reflection on how various materials within software documentation can influence user engagement and comprehension, noting the significant distinction between substantive and discarded text across different segments of Allplan software documentation.</data>
