      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Exchanging Data with Other Programs refers to processes that allow different software applications to share or transfer information effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Exchanging Data with Other Programs is a title that outlines mechanisms for data transfer between various CAD application interfaces and formats, specifically mentioning DWG, DXF, and DGN formats.&lt;SEP&gt;Exchanging data with other programs is a title that likely serves as an introduction to the discussion surrounding data transfer methodologies between various systems.&lt;SEP&gt;Exchanging data with other programs is a discarded content title indicating a key aspect of interoperability in data exchange between architectural software and other applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Exchanging Data with Other Programs is a discarded content section that discusses methods for data exchange using Allplan software.</data>
