    <node id="Interoperability">
      <data key="d0">Interoperability</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Interoperability refers to the ability of different systems to work together, a theme central to managing and transforming design data effectively across platforms.&lt;SEP&gt;Interoperability is a principle that allows different systems and software to work together, especially in the context of data exchanges.&lt;SEP&gt;Interoperability refers to the capability of Allplan software to exchange data with external applications effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Interoperability refers to the ability of different systems to work together and share data effectively, which is relevant to the discussion of Allplan.</data>
