      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Captions are text annotations that accompany images and provide various descriptions or titles that enhance understanding or context. In the current instance, it is noted that there are no captions provided alongside any images. This lack of accompanying text means that there are no additional explanations or contextual information available in this analysis.

The role of captions generally involves offering descriptive text that can illuminate important details or explain aspects of the images. Captions serve to clarify or enhance the viewer's comprehension of the visual content. In this case, however, it is emphasized that no such text annotations are present, underscoring a significant absence of descriptive information. 

There was a mention that captions could include previews or coordinates related to various offsets that define new points, yet this is not applicable here due to the absence of any captions. Overall, the descriptions consistently highlight the absence of captions, reinforcing the conclusion that no supplementary text is available to aid understanding.</data>
