    <node id="Functional Context">
      <data key="d0">Functional Context</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Functional Context relates to the operational environment in which file interfaces and settings are applied within CAD systems.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4c8791dcb306d3419c6dc1f6d3bb00c</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896633</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Technical Specifications">
      <data key="d0">Technical Specifications</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Technical Specifications refer to the detailed information provided within the Element Information Window regarding design elements, including attributes like 'Format', 'Pen thickness', and 'Line type'.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical specifications cover details and requirements essential for understanding and implementing features in architectural design.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical Specifications are guidelines regarding the interfaces used for file exporting and importing in CAD environments.&lt;SEP&gt;Technical specifications outline the mechanisms, attributes, and settings necessary for effective data handling in IFC standards.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4c8791dcb306d3419c6dc1f6d3bb00c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abf8f6db1ed82992e31819aa27952c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58e9cff5567cd20bfe51b22a5d56be2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a27839fe34b8ded0988268a250aab5d</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896633</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Data Exchange">
      <data key="d0">Data Exchange</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Data exchange refers to a section within the User Manual discussing methods for transferring data between different systems or formats.&lt;SEP&gt;Data exchange refers to the process of transferring data between CAD applications, which is a significant feature addressed in the user manual.&lt;SEP&gt;Data exchange is a feature in ProjectPilot facilitating the transfer of information between documents and users.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Exchange involves the transferability of files and settings between CAD applications, significant for interoperability.&lt;SEP&gt;Data exchange refers to the process of transferring data between different software programs, underscoring the importance of interoperability in architectural practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Data exchange refers to the transfer and interoperability of information between different programs, particularly in the context of architectural software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-d4c8791dcb306d3419c6dc1f6d3bb00c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5052fbe47433325630129ce02ea9467c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f28858a62c0a7e051c948c0bad73c62b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a6c7b27b30480dab8361768f8b225f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd7e68faef5a44c498363c7227d75afe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4526a3914ff00c77819d612514b265fb</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896634</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Line Styles">
      <data key="d0">Line Styles</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Line Styles showcase various representations such as continuous, dashed, and dotted lines, which are crucial for visual communication in drawings.&lt;SEP&gt;Line styles are design elements discussed in the text that pertain to formatting within the instructions.&lt;SEP&gt;Line styles are various graphical representations used in software environments, mentioned in the context of providing instructions on Page 133.&lt;SEP&gt;Line Styles refer to the visual representation of lines in design software, integral to project methodologies that describe element interactions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-7098321c2776e7e778c6bbb3c1ca42a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19807915ea52d6607cd1aa32207d700a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80239c7e79b07f28228b17e3d25b4a91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0041828ceff3158c0eb1286bf8b2c9d2</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896634</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Documentations">
      <data key="d0">Documentations</data>
      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">Documentations encompass structured information provided to guide users through software functionalities and operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Documentations encompass guidelines and instructions related to data exporting processes, including potential errors and ensuring file compatibility.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c17ca9cd7bd4432fdbf6fdcb784862b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f84da255ee65289eac9859c276de7150</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896635</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Data Exporting Processes">
      <data key="d0">Data Exporting Processes</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Data exporting processes involve methods and practices for transferring data from one system or format to another, focusing on user guidance and error management.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c17ca9cd7bd4432fdbf6fdcb784862b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896635</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="File Formats">
      <data key="d0">File Formats</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">File Formats, such as .xml and .bak, indicate the types of files created and used in BIM for configurations and settings.&lt;SEP&gt;File formats refer to the various structures used for saving data, including DWG, DXF, and DGN, that are crucial for data exchange in design software.&lt;SEP&gt;File formats represent the structure and organization of data files, influencing compatibility and handling procedures in software applications.&lt;SEP&gt;File formats refer to the various types of file extensions associated with digital documents, indicating how data is stored and used in different applications.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c17ca9cd7bd4432fdbf6fdcb784862b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b859f32c9b3b8de597221d3bd8e692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db3527e684a25b932d0774c8848b1ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181d5076e84ba9cf81d6ed8940b0da7b</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896636</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Software Applications">
      <data key="d0">Software Applications</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">Software applications are programs designed to facilitate tasks, including handling data exporting and managing file formats.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-2c17ca9cd7bd4432fdbf6fdcb784862b</data>
