    <node id="Design Software">
      <data key="d0">Design Software</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Design Software refers to various applications specifically developed for creating, managing, and manipulating visual and design elements across different creative workflows. This software is utilized for a wide range of tasks, including architectural planning, graphic design, 3D modeling, and technical drawing, making it essential in fields such as architecture and engineering.

The key functionalities of Design Software include tools for editing graphic objects, managing layers, and creating user-friendly interfaces for design manipulation. Users can perform operations like layering, cursor snapping, and track line management, allowing for precise control over design elements. The software often includes an Objects palette and features for hierarchical sorting, which help in organizing and navigating design content effectively.

Design Software encompasses functionalities that facilitate the creation of both 2D and 3D designs, enabling users to visualize and modify architectural features, layouts, and detailed drawings. It provides essential tools for navigating design spaces and managing viewports, which are particularly relevant for model manipulation tasks. Additionally, many applications within this category include options for exporting designs in various formats, including print-ready files and PDFs.

Furthermore, Design Software integrates features focused on improving workflow efficiency, such as Smart Symbols for streamlined processes, filtering options based on visual properties like color, and robust management of layer properties. This comprehensive suite of functionalities makes Design Software indispensable for professionals aiming for technical accuracy and aesthetic fidelity in their design projects.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-bd8e342afc7b46634cae508eaa15f52f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d2bcf1c612666251acc2f53393922b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d58e9cff5567cd20bfe51b22a5d56be2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9b50e123581bdee43b66d303dc87450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57b0a705b4c516ae369d9cb201b7064b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cab00b8e8a73fee64ae77a8cb78d4c51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-841ddeeb367db179e52e136890e7970a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aebf14603361df3e4efb47aa37cf81d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe9f0600b71ac1fb6333f1bc72307a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c09617e15dd11f9c3628b9ef27539f55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf22ff3619e3c74d2dd26a17af795473&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0d386adbd9913ab17eb1c6d28ef44e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e344a98fd7e3b130812427e0823b8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7371c601a5243c554f050195081be62b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9325818914688bfadc51b8235805e01a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aae1bd537c874a4ba7239994e1e13a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-061fb125d2fb8a19e5a7710ea6cde4cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d222e0ba3ea158698894e838b854e877&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b017821f74da660f504741df548bcb16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-206284cb471f7df3622f47c3aa59e408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60c363ac1543df296a0116c60c083334&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16c3ff24d49635597ef23c085a868247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f93dfe57c8fc90fa6d294b523bed3995&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0f82e0207f6c5657ed5590659ca3d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e637fc0a6aaa19a2e54eef0d67d0638&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9045f88951f48755aaeac249e8f66da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a5fb3518984234d6291e952cf809e13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b5581edd6a5150ce2ec40420195a45b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a2bfca4e7776125bad53ee8820e666&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c32800b93fbfcf403671e77c76a3080&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e495b0cd79cc88f595fa746df2e7844&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8760942d27bd57853f623d22dcb381ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8924a78340ea4369a0687057b5776b4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1d3b892e5fac15fa1b00797afb5d1ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-432c5af8d43543063d571a883e445d9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e7665397f8da420cacc22e54396eb6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df468dd2b4c09a7898dde72cf5e2c629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92300d8d13610cc91f200a7a30321c2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2be476b4c50c0ded1655c03aa85ca153&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935cacdbf30f098651e73da157d12d60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17df94c5e8bc7