    <node id="Selection Methods">
      <data key="d0">Selection Methods</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Selection Methods refer to a variety of techniques and processes used within Allplan software for efficiently selecting elements or features. These methods facilitate user interaction and enhance workflow efficiency by providing an array of selection options.

Key selection techniques include conventional methods like click selection, as well as regional fencing, which allows users to select multiple items within a defined area. Other specified methods encompass grouped elements and the use of rectangular or bracket selections, enabling a more streamlined selection of graphical elements. Users can also select specific documents through different approaches, such as single item selection, selecting a series, or defining a range.

The instructional content and user manual detail these selection methods comprehensively, ensuring that users can effectively navigate and manipulate elements in the design context. Overall, Selection Methods are crucial for optimizing user experience and operational effectiveness within Allplan’s design environment.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-80239c7e79b07f28228b17e3d25b4a91&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60924b3ac3c586e850d1e42321678547&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed5028e99a41cecaca997e431e97801a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b043aca48744d9fa6699c3bb61efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bbbcc35b4506d6db0cc8328718d4891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b91420bc378d72e2410737951741eaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae8832a2783b4ebb13fc2190697157d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64220d8c6a507cb0154d5cab89b3a5f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc8996e98416f918dd41d6db22638f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-badee94ea3a627e760da71db876d2f67</data>
