      <data key="d0">IFC Interface</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The IFC Interface refers to the capabilities related to data export and integration, indicated as significant for users needing detailed guidance.&lt;SEP&gt;The IFC Interface is a title that introduces a section focused on Industry Foundation Classes used in building data modeling.&lt;SEP&gt;The IFC Interface is a framework for importing and exporting data, though content regarding its functionalities on page 278 is missing.&lt;SEP&gt;IFC Interface refers to a high-level label for a section on IFC export functionalities within a software environment, likely Allplan, emphasizing data management and interoperability.</data>
