    <node id="Design Software Environment">
      <data key="d0">Design Software Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Design Software Environment refers to the digital platform where architectural tools are utilized for tasks like model modification and reference surface management.&lt;SEP&gt;Design Software Environment is the context where the Vertical Menu appears, facilitating user access to design tools based on interactions.&lt;SEP&gt;The design software environment includes discussions about tools and options that aid in user navigation and understanding.&lt;SEP&gt;Design Software Environment is the context within which selection tools are utilized, often involving graphical user interfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;Design Software Environment refers to the application context where users engage with various design tools and functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Design Software Environment encompasses the tools and interface used for interactive modification of design elements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1169d7ca37ca50c76f10adced882a3e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cd541abfc2c8f9eeb97e7c3caf2b5d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbe3718260bfb37d0523abccfd243ded&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1eb2086ae925574778cf33517c0d5538&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7efa2c94792e08136163d0b198a08a68&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2682cda91fcc66490a3823382618a08a</data>
