    <node id="Building Information Modeling (BIM)">
      <data key="d0">Building Information Modeling (BIM)</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Building Information Modeling (BIM) is a method that facilitates the organization of building information and integrates technologies for architectural design.&lt;SEP&gt;Building Information Modeling (BIM) is a foundational concept that enhances workflow efficiency and project organization within architectural practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Building Information Modeling (BIM) is a process that involves the generation and management of digital representations of physical and functional characteristics of places.&lt;SEP&gt;Building Information Modeling (BIM) is a method in construction that includes digital representations of physical and functional characteristics of places, often involving structural configurations and guidelines.&lt;SEP&gt;Building Information Modeling (BIM) is a process used for creating and managing information about a construction project across its lifecycle.</data>
