    <node id="Symbol">
      <data key="d0">Symbol</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The entity "Symbol" encompasses a range of mathematical and graphical notations that were mentioned in the discarded content. Each individual symbol has been described as lacking significant information or context, suggesting their limited relevance to the overall analysis.

One of the symbols noted is '$\\textcircled { + }$', which serves as a visual representation but provides minimal information independently. Similarly, the symbol '$\\fallingdotseq$' is categorized as an isolated element, also found within the discarded content but without substantive context. Another symbol, '$\\gg$', is highlighted as a mathematical or graphical notation that appears twice in the descriptions, reinforcing its unclear significance and lack of context for effective understanding.

The symbol ('$\\\\textmd { ‰}$') is identified as potentially relevant within a mathematical or engineering context, possibly functioning as a unit or marker in calculations. In contrast, the symbols '$\\circledast$' and '$\\circledast$' are both noted as lacking substantive meaning, with one explicitly termed a formatting error or placeholder and the other described as irrelevant to the discourse.

Lastly, the symbol '$\\nwarrow$' is mentioned as a misplaced notation, failing to contribute meaningful information to discussions surrounding layer management. Overall, these symbols are characterized by their singular presence in the discarded content, often cited for their unclear meaning, and reflect the challenges of integrating various symbolic representations into coherent analytical discourse.</data>
