    <node id="Architectural Modeling">
      <data key="d0">Architectural Modeling</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Architectural Modeling is the process of creating digital representations of structures, which is supported by Allplan's software functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural modeling refers to the processes relevant to design and representation but is noted as not having a clear connection to the discarded mathematical symbol in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural Modeling involves the application of design principles through the software tool, requiring a good understanding of installation and drawing techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural Modeling is the practice of creating representations of buildings and structures, involving discussions that could enhance user understanding of related tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural Modeling involves the representation and planning of structures, emphasizing the importance of standards and compliance.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural Modeling relates to the design and configuration processes in architecture, focusing on how structures are utilized and organized.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural modeling refers to the process of creating representations of buildings and structures, often involving software like Allplan for accurate data manipulation.</data>
