    <node id="Key Elements">
      <data key="d0">Key Elements</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Key Elements refer to the main attributes discussed in the discarded content, including selection preview colors and user interface functions.&lt;SEP&gt;Key elements of precision drawing include definitions, techniques, and implications of precision in the design process.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Elements are essential components outlined in the analysis that include the purpose and functionalities of OLE objects.&lt;SEP&gt;Key elements involve the benefits and operations of XRefs, emphasizing dynamic updating and interaction with other software components.&lt;SEP&gt;Key elements refer to the important components discussed in surrounding content, such as comparisons of tools, organizational hierarchy, and significance of drawing files.&lt;SEP&gt;Key Elements refer to essential components in the broader context of print layout management, including diversified printing options and settings in the Print Preview tool.</data>
