    <node id="Icons">
      <data key="d0">Icons</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">Icons are graphical representations used in various sections of the Allplan user interface, notably within the Actionbar, Properties Palette, and toolbars. They convey a plethora of functionalities related to architecture and design, thereby enhancing user interaction and efficiency. 

In the Actionbar, icons signify different architectural tools and actions, while the Properties Palette utilizes icons to represent functions such as zooming, searching, and filtering. The toolbar icons allow users to create new objects, access libraries, and perform various other operations, characterized by a minimalist design that prioritizes clarity and usability. 

Specifically, icons within the toolbar symbolize functions like 'Undo', 'Redo', 'Open/Save', 'Visibility/Hide', and 'Layout/Grid View’. These graphic elements often have a pixelated appearance, aligning with the aesthetic needs of digital design. 

Further representations are found in the Input Options Toolbar, which focuses on drawing or modifying polylines and geometric shapes, and in specific sections labeled Create and Change, where icons explicitly assist with design tasks. Each icon comprises unique geometric patterns and symbols, encapsulated within small square areas, enhancing precision in drawing functionalities. 

Overall, icons play a crucial role in the architectural software interface, streamlining various design and manipulation processes for users.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-635fd814c6fa873c7ea06d7e51a4a309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a7ea0fcb7e0ea1b9aea375b2f66e37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b24b6e9ff5efe2556c3f3e17d46e51e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d151fbf9ee7fcf19701b9dc546ac85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56e7a8afa3dd440debe7bcb5405bda63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e460aed26fb282e994fcabf167369c99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-968e07c63e20bbac8007492be7a90dbb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65e5b17292bf5aeb0da70a4a5ccdb7d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a006a6c963e8781295b7d58c913f54fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c36ab84e987861cbb78ee2d63372f5cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032462a24ce269c64a42e612a0c5a765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0938efbf06e3d980c6f900e209b135c5</data>
