    <node id="Print Preview">
      <data key="d0">Print Preview</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Print Preview is a feature found in Allplan 2020 that provides users with the capability to view and assess documents before they are printed. This tool is designed to ensure that both the layout and content are presented as intended, allowing for any necessary adjustments to be made in document display and printer settings. 

The Print Preview functionality allows users to visualize how the document will look when printed, which is crucial for achieving printing accuracy and confirming that margins and other settings are appropriate. This feature plays a vital role in the user experience by enabling individuals to make informed decisions about adjustments needed prior to initiating the printing process. 

In addition to its primary function, the term "Print Preview" can also refer to various options and settings related to managing how documents are prepared for printing, although this aspect is less detailed in the descriptions provided. Overall, Print Preview serves as an essential tool within software applications like Allplan 2020, facilitating a smoother and more accurate printing workflow.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-38a8a82f299e74e7da1ede2ee18ded75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a9714aa009a544e12d91b6e75a4d150&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa75c080b391647ebd8ea4ffd9a169c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f586273ea6a7044dc7604e4df904101&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c22b0ab29996692a50409c6be635eb1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1962d204e1d817c225b43c979be9e11f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2938bd952ac9fb2a762941c3969e71e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1965c98263f5c7c9fc33b28a1e254b12</data>
