    <node id="Print Settings">
      <data key="d0">Print Settings</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Print Settings are associated with the operational details in the text and highlight the functionalities expected from Allplan 2020.&lt;SEP&gt;Print settings refer to the various configurable options available to users when preparing a document for printing, including margins, headers, footers, and more.&lt;SEP&gt;Print Settings encompass various configurable aspects regarding how documents are printed, including printer selection and layout adjustments.&lt;SEP&gt;Print settings refer to configuration options in software that determine the scale, margins, and presentation of elements during printing.&lt;SEP&gt;Print Settings refer to the configuration options and parameters that may influence the layout or presentation of printed material and are discussed in relation to the discarded content.&lt;SEP&gt;Print settings refer to configurations that determine how documents are printed, likely mentioned in relation to user interface functionalities.</data>
