    <node id="Design Workflows">
      <data key="d0">Design Workflows</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Design Workflows encompass the processes and techniques that facilitate efficient design operations within the software.&lt;SEP&gt;Design workflows are the processes that users follow in drafting and design, which may be affected by clipboard operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Design workflows refer to the processes in architectural design where format properties play a significant role for visual clarity and efficient outputs.&lt;SEP&gt;Design workflows involve the structured processes and procedures engineered for streamlined design and drafting tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Design workflows refer to structured processes that enhance efficiency in design tasks through optimized management of design elements.&lt;SEP&gt;Design workflows refer to the structured processes involved in managing design elements, where smart symbols play a critical role.&lt;SEP&gt;Design Workflows represent the structured procedures followed in design processes to enhance efficiency and effectiveness in CAD environments.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dff48bbd50e8c71258164f30093ef33a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96f432670260a4683e8787869f7b743b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-faeaf8539bb14f11d320aeb0b7950e3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25d432a54bd43de035f3c24c5aa0e961&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c1bb94e215bb8cbbc9805b15edd42f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcab7bf36d42e74a9733b00a931b4332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71e3f5ebf7cde66ad5148c0ed23c755c</data>
