    <node id="Design Application">
      <data key="d0">Design Application</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Design Application is a category of software designed to assist users in creating, modifying, and managing design elements within various visual contexts. It typically features a viewport toolbar that enables functionalities such as selection and zooming, thus enhancing user interaction in graphical design. However, certain limitations exist due to a lack of content and structural information, which can affect usability.

This software environment is essential for tasks related to architectural and urban planning, where it facilitates the manipulation of geometrical elements and coordinates. It includes various tools and methods that help manage visual representations effectively. The Design Application also incorporates filtering functionalities to streamline design processes, ensuring that users can efficiently navigate and engage with the elements they are working on.

Overall, the Design Application serves multiple purposes, catering to different aspects of design work—from geometric manipulation to user interaction management—providing a versatile platform for designers across different fields.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-27445d4e2ca5605036cf7d358169817c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25e2edd3351791ee282bb1709ab6bbfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd5336772abb1e6a10869aa4432fd948&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26eea2337a9b0e6bfc83be0bfb32ac61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21db218c2681f002d58d92e06ee2c364&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bea38be07796088a8eca302175fdabcd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8daee81a82bc56c6132a8fc83c0c42a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7aa2de35051a07440a4fda92b2ec401c</data>
