    <node id="Shortcut Menus">
      <data key="d0">Shortcut Menus</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Shortcut menus are features in user interfaces that provide quick access to frequently used functions or tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Shortcut Menus are part of the user interface and are discussed in relation to various modes (Design and Navigation) and their functionality.&lt;SEP&gt;Shortcut Menus are tools within software applications that provide quick access to various functions and features through right-click options or keyboard shortcuts.&lt;SEP&gt;Shortcut Menus are contextual menus that provide quick access to various commands and functions within software applications.&lt;SEP&gt;Shortcut Menus are tools mentioned in the context of information likely following the discarded content, indicating user interface elements in architecture.&lt;SEP&gt;Shortcut menus are additional features within the software interface that enhance user accessibility and provide quick access to tools and functions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-f38cf3ba0f8cec23986e4542fb4b7a73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abc4489156f7338736e4a38b8b10cc98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1f742bc5c2405867e1d1c35c4b7860c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fdbc7e19fe5f9d99f4b190011e5d5a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6fd7e1d1f9713baf8bbdc66e7b032e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fbffcefc317d0a7ea08df02ff6f2536</data>
