    <node id="Data Structuring">
      <data key="d0">Data Structuring</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Data structuring involves organizing and managing architectural data, which is a key theme discussed in relation to Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Structuring refers to the methods and principles used to organize and manage data efficiently, particularly in contexts like Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Data Structuring is a concept that emphasizes the organization and management of data within projects to enhance workflow efficiency.&lt;SEP&gt;Data structuring involves methodologies for organizing and handling information, especially in relation to drawing files within building structures.&lt;SEP&gt;Data structuring refers to the principles and methodologies for organizing and overseeing project data effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;Data structuring refers to the principles and methodologies for categorizing documents effectively within ProjectPilot.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-393e11bde9bd0e1d6cc3a370c4650376&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59b7bf09cf4a352e9493ab3525a3ace7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfe9f0600b71ac1fb6333f1bc72307a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ad4e42e291dfe47f37fc019d0db099b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09cc853c0929848d59ac804c43580402&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e81eca64c42f550b12f0f82c5610f7</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
      <data key="d5">1763896701</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="BIM Practices">
      <data key="d0">BIM Practices</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">BIM practices refer to methodologies for managing data in Building Information Modeling, as highlighted in the context surrounding the discarded content.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-393e11bde9bd0e1d6cc3a370c4650376</data>
