    <node id="3D Modeling">
      <data key="d0">3D Modeling</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">3D Modeling refers to the techniques and tools available within the Allplan software for creating three-dimensional representations.&lt;SEP&gt;3D modeling refers to the process of creating a three-dimensional representation of an object using specialized software.&lt;SEP&gt;3D Modeling encompasses the techniques and processes involved in creating a three-dimensional representation of objects using specialized software.&lt;SEP&gt;3D modeling is a process discussed in the context related to various functionalities and tools, such as element selection, light settings, and camera paths.&lt;SEP&gt;3D Modeling is the process of creating a three-dimensional representation of a surface or object using special software.&lt;SEP&gt;3D modeling is a contextual area in which the functionalities of Allplan, like lighting and camera path, are relevant.&lt;SEP&gt;3D modeling is a process involving the creation of two-dimensional and three-dimensional objects using specialized software and techniques related to lighting, camera functionalities, and rendering.</data>
