    <node id="Drawing File Statuses">
      <data key="d0">Drawing File Statuses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Drawing file statuses relate to the various states of the files in a project, crucial for efficient management of design resources.&lt;SEP&gt;Drawing file statuses refer to the different conditions or states of drawing files that affect how they can be managed and edited within a design project.&lt;SEP&gt;Drawing file statuses refer to the current conditions or attributes of drawing files within a specific software environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Drawing file statuses are an important aspect of the Allplan software that affects editing and visibility of files.&lt;SEP&gt;Drawing file statuses refer to the states or conditions of drawing files that are discussed in the manual or guide.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-dbbd564c80da8a545228ae041a60c486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-656c6ea66b577915e78e14b99fcff201&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d1820b0451b7572f068cd0be91559b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17583b10964c1e5e228f4f3703d84910&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ece46ef6a59033ba429c3ebe8b86a98</data>
