      <data key="d2">User Actions refer to the interactions users can have with library items and folders in the Allplan software.&lt;SEP&gt;User Actions denote the tasks performed by users when interacting with software tools and interfaces.&lt;SEP&gt;User Actions refer to the interactions needed to modify format properties in Allplan, essential for utilizing the software effectively.&lt;SEP&gt;User actions pertain to the tasks and operations that individuals carry out when managing drawing files, which necessitate clarity for effective navigation.&lt;SEP&gt;User actions encompass the steps and methods employed by individuals to manage documents effectively within a software system.&lt;SEP&gt;User Actions refer to the tasks or steps users take to achieve designated objectives within the procedural context.</data>
