    <node id="Δx">
      <data key="d0">Δx</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Δx is a key data field within the dialog line in design software, primarily representing the directional offset along the x-axis. The default setting indicates a value of 0.0000, suggesting no offset for horizontal measurement. As a numerical input field, Δx serves as a critical parameter that influences positioning within the software interface.

While Δx is typically set to 0.0000, it is also associated with various numerical values depending on the context. For instance, it can appear as '2*4' in an interface, facilitating calculations related to point manipulation. There are instances where Δx may be highlighted with other values, such as 1.3576, which further indicates its role as a variable representing positional adjustments along the x-axis. Additionally, Δx serves as a label for a text field showing a horizontal offset value, sometimes marked at '2.0000'.

In conclusion, Δx encapsulates several functionalities related to directional offsets in the design software, integrating user input and mathematical calculations to guide positioning accurately.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-56e0d709a61c2954fff181af06317028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6ce70dad379ae311b37a838efcb486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aabedbf5693787b17fe880f480ac3f40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c926d8f34f6208bc9f906828d61e12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6bb3704ef3f257e8d32aef88dafc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a006a6c963e8781295b7d58c913f54fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53a559f748b3bdf7387cf1b1f8ee8d46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bbc08c2a5e06f66f57db63ec4c7c00</data>
