    <node id="Δy">
      <data key="d0">Δy</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Δy is a multifaceted data field used within a software interface, specifically within the Dialog Line and Dialog Line Box context. It primarily serves as a variable representing directional offset along the y-axis, offering users the ability to input positional adjustments in design software. The most commonly referenced value for Δy is 0.0000, indicating no current offset for vertical measurements. 

Additionally, Δy also appears to serve as a numerical input field where users can set specific values for vertical displacement, including measurements that affect overall positioning within the software environment. Notably, other values such as 11.0274 have been mentioned in the dialog box, highlighting varying adjustments that may be applicable in different instances.

The label for Δy sometimes represents alternative calculations for point manipulation within the interface, where it is set to '4/3' in specific contexts, indicating that it can take on different roles depending on the specific user requirement. Moreover, a different context presents Δy as representing a vertical offset value of '3', showcasing its adaptability within varying input scenarios.

Overall, Δy serves as an essential parameter for users to define vertical displacements and adjustments in graphical environments, fundamental for precise control over design layouts and positioning tasks.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-56e0d709a61c2954fff181af06317028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6ce70dad379ae311b37a838efcb486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aabedbf5693787b17fe880f480ac3f40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c926d8f34f6208bc9f906828d61e12a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b6bb3704ef3f257e8d32aef88dafc86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a006a6c963e8781295b7d58c913f54fd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53a559f748b3bdf7387cf1b1f8ee8d46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80bbc08c2a5e06f66f57db63ec4c7c00</data>
