    <node id="Functionalities">
      <data key="d0">Functionalities</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Functionalities refer to the specific capabilities and features offered by Allplan software, enhancing users' ability to perform various tasks effectively. These functionalities encompass a range of tools designed for navigating and managing library elements as well as user interfaces within the application. 

Particularly, functionalities related to plane models are central to the software's performance, providing users with essential features that facilitate modifications and enhancements in design. For instance, specific operations include inserting or replacing reference surfaces, which are crucial for model adjustments related to Allplan's Building Information Modeling (BIM) capabilities.

Overall, functionalities within Allplan are aimed at supporting user tasks and improving productivity. They are integral to design mode interactions, offering a suite of tools tailored for effective manipulation and customization of objects throughout the design process. This comprehensive set of features ensures that users can undertake their tasks with increased efficiency and precision.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-4ae19b702daf07ba3b17255e4bed9db2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4523e049fc00468e44d53f5c090def24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7218ce75fb6c97ea782e69e9400ae3ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78d14420ea310712e7951bafcf032e21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ef06de7e10a2aa7e4cdbc38635d7cd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2785c23eea558e541a95481334ca5baa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e36969f4f63b7e40cff66adc31e252fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b714bcb576d1d7af19a195bad055535</data>
