    <node id="Polylines">
      <data key="d0">Polylines</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Polylines are a type of graphic representation that involves connecting multiple line segments, mentioned in the context of input options.&lt;SEP&gt;Polylines are graphical entities that users can create within the software environment through specific interaction techniques.&lt;SEP&gt;Polylines are design elements that allow users to draw shapes and lines within design tools.&lt;SEP&gt;Polylines represent a series of connected lines used in design software for drawing shapes and defining areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Polylines are geometric tools used in architectural design for creating lines that represent shapes and areas, crucial for accurate design representation.&lt;SEP&gt;Polylines are geometric shapes that can be manipulated within Allplan, crucial for design and architectural tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;Polylines are essential design entities used in area detection techniques which require user manipulation within CAD software.</data>
