    <node id="Toolbar">
      <data key="d0">Toolbar</data>
      <data key="d1">artifact</data>
      <data key="d2">The Toolbar is a graphical user interface (GUI) element integral to the Allplan application, positioned prominently at the top of the interface. It is designed to enhance user interaction by providing a range of icons that facilitate various software actions. These actions include essential functions such as opening projects, accessing print settings, and performing design tasks.

Within the Toolbar, users can find specific buttons for creating new groups, inserting elements, and managing object functionalities pertinent to Allplan. It serves as a comprehensive control panel for executing commands related to design operations. Notably, part of the Toolbar is labeled 'Layers,' which contains tabs showcasing distinct functionalities that assist users in their design tasks.

The Toolbar also includes essential options for modifying graphical elements, such as buttons for 'Undo,' 'Redo,' and 'Delete,' which are critical for effective design management. Additionally, there are input options specifically for handling polylines, indicating the Toolbar's versatility in catering to various design requirements.

Overall, the Toolbar is a fundamental component of the Allplan user interface, centralizing access to a multitude of functions and features that streamline user interaction and improve workflow efficiency in the design software.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-005d6e213ff60df2f8e1b0d009ada5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d151fbf9ee7fcf19701b9dc546ac85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56e7a8afa3dd440debe7bcb5405bda63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82c29a2b5b27e0270d07760e7f57c200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c421d3a263fd1ce84ca9208be184443c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7fc974dab9ec36ae9be4cff86d42d3e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-733638abd7ec99e44a6cfa99ee6014c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457310acfac309d1e67d5e85d5af5e09</data>
