    <node id="Plane Models">
      <data key="d0">Plane Models</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Plane Models refer to various representations associated with aircraft designs and architectural building projects, encompassing a wide range of applications in technical documentation and design methodologies. In the context of aviation, Plane Models denote specific aircraft designs or types that necessitate a thorough understanding of installation and operational procedures.

In architecture and construction, Plane Models symbolize specific types of models employed within Building Information Modeling (BIM) that are crucial for architectural design and building construction. These models serve as essential tools for visualizing and managing different aspects of building projects, focusing on configurations that impact structural integration and functionality. They facilitate discussions about architectural representations that interact with building structures in design projects and their essential role in effective design practices.

Furthermore, Plane Models are integrated into software management capabilities, particularly within applications like Allplan, where they represent urban architecture or planning structures. The models emphasize their organizational and functional aspects, illustrating their importance in managing architectural data and enhancing the efficiency of design processes. 

Overall, Plane Models play a vital role across various domains, from managing technical configurations within aviation to enabling effective architectural design through spatial relationships and detailed representations in CAD design. They bridge the gap between technical documentation and practical application in both aviation and building project contexts.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1db3527e684a25b932d0774c8848b1ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-044d7e159b5566456d267a51e9c7fa44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9add4b1a1710511eb95f28026e2db24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb4d0444551f3d03177577b98c36a13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcf7577d0b90f6ba71954ba050cc5d48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2d88ddfd727f7f87635e963bbfd6d1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01630897320d912d860c0ed5a7baa406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b69eba9c0738e7d77ce7d1a0d74e58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f50dd1af58390ee1ecc8e2d2e6426aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-895e7a5e80f106b50d21886d5083d4c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4bbee4ee13047cc84385a1de2d0ad5c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec761b3324cf1c962b2d427a74fd8cd2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcf5201c4754f24330861a154c0a0b9e</data>
      <data key="d4">Allplan_2020_Manual.pdf</data>
