      <data key="d0">Visibility Settings</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Visibility settings are functionalities concerning how graphical elements are displayed to users within the user interface.&lt;SEP&gt;Visibility Settings pertain to user-defined parameters that determine how objects are displayed or interacted with within a software context.&lt;SEP&gt;Visibility Settings are parameters in the Allplan software that influence how layers are displayed or interacted with in architectural designs.&lt;SEP&gt;Visibility settings determine how elements are displayed in design software, affecting clarity and user interaction.&lt;SEP&gt;Visibility settings are methods within software that control which elements are shown or hidden during operation.</data>
