      <data key="d0">CAD Environment</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The CAD Environment is a computer-aided design setting where users manipulate 3D objects and manage their visibility and transparency.&lt;SEP&gt;The CAD environment is the context in which design elements are displayed and manipulated using software like Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;The CAD Environment encompasses the digital workspace where computer-aided design tasks are performed, allowing for various operations such as point snapping.&lt;SEP&gt;CAD environment encompasses the digital workspace where users operate design software for architectural and engineering purposes.&lt;SEP&gt;The CAD environment refers to the digital platform where computer-aided design is performed, involving various methodologies and tools.&lt;SEP&gt;The CAD environment is a digital design space where layers and planes are utilized for project management.</data>
