    <node id="Architectural Layouts">
      <data key="d0">Architectural Layouts</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Architectural layouts refer to the systematic arrangement of elements in architectural design, relevant to the study of hatching.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural layouts pertain to the arrangements and designs of structures, influencing how hatching properties function in visual representations.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural layouts involve representations that require proper hatching for effective communication of design intent.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural layouts are structured designs that depict the organization and arrangement of spaces and elements in a building or site.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural layouts are plans or arrangements used in architecture, discussing how patterns can be applied within designs.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural Layouts are designs or plans outlining the arrangement and organization of spaces and elements within a structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Architectural layouts encompass the design and arrangement of patterns or components in architectural spaces.</data>
