    <node id="Usability">
      <data key="d0">Usability</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Usability pertains to how effectively users can interact with the user interface, which is essential for maximizing engagement with Allplan's functionalities.&lt;SEP&gt;Usability refers to the effectiveness and efficiency with which users can navigate and customize software interfaces, such as in Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Usability refers to ease of use and efficiency in navigating the software's interface, affecting user experience and preference.&lt;SEP&gt;Usability pertains to how easily users can navigate and learn the interface, enhancing their interaction with Allplan.&lt;SEP&gt;Usability is the quality of the experience of a user when interacting with a product, particularly how intuitive and effective the interface is.&lt;SEP&gt;Usability refers to how effectively symbols and design elements can be used within design software, emphasizing efficiency in workflows.&lt;SEP&gt;Usability relates to the ease with which users can interact with ProjectPilot, particularly in managing project documents.</data>
