    <node id="Viewport Tools">
      <data key="d0">Viewport Tools</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Viewport Tools refer to a set of specific functionalities designed for effectively managing content display areas, particularly within software applications focused on visual representation and manipulation of design entities. These tools are integral to 3D navigation and perspective adjustments, helping users manipulate graphical interfaces and various design elements within architectural software.

The functionalities of Viewport Tools include navigation and display manipulation features such as scaling options, different view types, and visibility controls. These aspects facilitate user interaction with design elements in a digital workspace, enhancing the overall experience of managing visual outputs. As highlighted in the documentation, these tools are essential for navigating and managing design entities effectively.

Moreover, Viewport Tools play a critical role in assisting users with understanding the installation process necessary for effective usage. They are typically accessible through the viewport toolbar, providing the means for users to manipulate and control their digital environments seamlessly. Overall, Viewport Tools are indispensable not only for managing display views but also for enhancing user engagement with design workflows.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-c31e5d279b3f3068c566e1b7da435ef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-643c1e9e2f3369670d259a1678cfaccc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-910efe40ae420cf9a62bc952e98be475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c75f8f337295af3186f163c6ffe1116b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0de891ca1f9321929a8bc785c2c1b10a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c0eb1d4d25fa9ce0f05f5c0cfd1bdd45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c46ec334a5537671d0130ddf1f37b6da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e60e08936a9c34cbeef4c292ce8e7f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b90194951b22f7e396d80356b767bd94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a7201b42518a0bdb1cf0a28a5df34b2</data>
