    <edge source="Allplan 2020" target="Allplan">
      <data key="d7">30.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Allplan 2020 is a specific version of the Allplan software, a Computer-Aided Design (CAD) tool developed by the company Allplan. This version not only represents a significant iteration within the series of Allplan software releases, but also indicates various updates, advancements in functionality and usability, and specific features relevant to tasks such as project management and architectural design.

As a reference point, Allplan 2020 is used to help users navigate the software's functionalities and understand its developmental phase. It is essential for operational procedures and highlights distinctive features and performance improvements made in design navigation. Furthermore, while the version itself acts as a context for documentation and operational details, some descriptions suggest that Allplan 2020 may lack sufficient context in certain discussions, rendering its significance less impactful in those instances.

Allplan, the organization behind this software version, is recognized for its continuous improvement and evolution of the Allplan series. As a version reference, Allplan 2020 ensures that users are aligned with the updates and features that differentiate this iteration from its predecessors and successors. It serves both as a title within the framework of documentation and operational guidelines, and as a crucial identifier in discussions centered around the Allplan software ecosystem.</data>
