    <edge source="Allplan" target="PythonParts">
      <data key="d7">9.0</data>
      <data key="d8">The relation "Allplan, PythonParts" refers to a functionality within Allplan, a software for architectural modeling, that supports the use of PythonParts for custom scripting. PythonParts are designed to enhance the modeling aspects of design by enabling the creation of parametric objects through Python scripts. This integration allows users to leverage programming for greater design capabilities and automation in various modeling tasks.

PythonParts significantly contribute to the programmable features of Allplan, facilitating streamlined design processes and enhancing overall functionality. They are a key component within Allplan, providing tools that aid in workflow optimization and increase efficiency in design execution. The presence of PythonParts is also highlighted in the user manuals, indicating their importance in the software’s operational context.

Additionally, PythonParts have a thematic connection to visual scripting within Allplan, suggesting that both functionalities can coexist to augment the user experience through enhanced automation and customization capabilities.</data>
