    <edge source="Image Content Analysis" target="Visual Analysis">
      <data key="d7">23.0</data>
      <data key="d8">Image Content Analysis and Visual Analysis are interrelated concepts within the field of image examination. Image Content Analysis serves as a broader framework that incorporates Visual Analysis as a key methodology for understanding the content of images. Through this relationship, Image Content Analysis emphasizes the evaluation and interpretation of various visual elements present in images, allowing for a deeper understanding of their structural and design features.

Visual Analysis focuses specifically on the examination of visual components, playing a crucial role in how Image Content Analysis interprets images. This method is utilized to assess not only the aesthetics but also the functional aspects of graphical elements, such as software interfaces, thereby enabling insights into their configuration and layout. Image Content Analysis leverages Visual Analysis to review and derive meaning from the visual aspects depicted in an image, including elements like page dimensions and margins in design contexts.

The integration of Visual Analysis within Image Content Analysis indicates that both processes are not only connected but functionally dependent on one another. Image Content Analysis can be seen as the foundation that facilitates a more detailed Visual Analysis, leading to comprehensive evaluations of imagery and its components. This collaboration supports a methodical approach to interpreting the features and functionalities presented in images, ensuring a thorough understanding of the visual landscape. 

Overall, Image Content Analysis encompasses the process of Visual Analysis to provide a detailed framework for assessing the content, design, and overall context of images, adhering to best practices in the analysis of visual materials.</data>
